WEBVTT

00:15.015 --> 00:17.016
[theme music playing]

00:56.556 --> 01:00.977
LOVE NEXT DOOR

01:01.853 --> 01:02.937
[humming]

01:09.986 --> 01:10.820
What's this?

01:12.280 --> 01:14.365
Hye-suk's things must've got into my bag.

01:15.533 --> 01:18.328
What is this? It's all in English.

01:18.411 --> 01:22.624
Does she carry this around
to show off how she can read it?

01:22.707 --> 01:24.584
She's such a brat. [clicks tongue]

01:27.378 --> 01:28.463
[magazine rustling]

01:33.092 --> 01:34.427
"The…"

01:36.763 --> 01:38.473
[groans softly]

01:39.057 --> 01:43.853
Where was Seok-ryu's
old electronic dictionary?

01:50.401 --> 01:52.153
Why does she have so much medicine?

01:52.237 --> 01:53.238
[solemn music playing]

01:53.321 --> 01:56.324
-[pills rattling]
-Are they all vitamins? What are these?

01:58.952 --> 02:01.287
Damn it. These are all in English too.

02:01.371 --> 02:02.372
[scoffs]

02:03.248 --> 02:04.833
[phone vibrating]

02:07.168 --> 02:08.002
HYE-SUK

02:08.086 --> 02:10.880
Jeez, you brat. Speak of the devil.

02:12.674 --> 02:13.716
Hey, Hye-suk.

02:14.717 --> 02:17.053
What? Seung-hyo's sick?

02:17.762 --> 02:20.723
-Thank you so much.
-[scoffs]

02:20.807 --> 02:22.600
He's sick.

02:22.684 --> 02:25.645
But how can I make him porridge?
I've never tried.

02:25.728 --> 02:29.315
You made a good decision.
He always gets sick around this time.

02:29.399 --> 02:30.650
-Really?
-Yeah.

02:30.733 --> 02:32.527
Strangely,
it's always in summer, not winter.

02:32.610 --> 02:34.487
He had a fever of 40 degrees once.

02:34.571 --> 02:37.198
Geun-sik and I had to carry him
to your husband's hospital.

02:37.282 --> 02:38.199
[exhales]

02:39.075 --> 02:40.702
By the way, I almost forgot.

02:40.785 --> 02:43.997
You left a magazine
written in English in my bag.

02:44.080 --> 02:45.039
A magazine?

02:45.582 --> 02:47.041
I never did that.

02:47.125 --> 02:48.459
You probably took it.

02:48.543 --> 02:51.588
Why would I take that? It's useless.

02:52.672 --> 02:55.008
-[Seung-hyo] We need to talk.
-[Seok-ryu] Let's talk later.

02:55.091 --> 02:56.885
I think Seok-ryu's inside.

02:57.927 --> 02:59.512
-Seok-ryu's here?
-Yeah.

02:59.596 --> 03:01.681
[Seung-hyo] How long
were you going to hide this for?

03:02.473 --> 03:04.100
Seung-hyo. [inhales]

03:04.601 --> 03:06.853
[voice shaking] This doesn't make sense.

03:07.770 --> 03:12.025
How could you go through something
like that without telling anyone?

03:15.486 --> 03:19.532
Stomach cancer surgery is serious.
How could you not tell anyone?

03:20.408 --> 03:21.618
[Mi-suk] Who has cancer?

03:23.202 --> 03:24.412
[door closes]

03:26.372 --> 03:27.874
[emotional music playing]

03:31.586 --> 03:33.588
[Mi-suk] I heard it from outside.

03:33.671 --> 03:34.547
Stomach cancer?

03:35.965 --> 03:37.425
Who has cancer?

03:43.723 --> 03:45.016
Who has cancer?

03:56.986 --> 03:58.112
Is it you?

04:05.328 --> 04:06.621
Is it really you?

04:11.918 --> 04:14.545
[whimpering]

04:17.131 --> 04:19.425
[both crying hysterically]

04:31.312 --> 04:32.605
[Seok-ryu crying]

04:43.032 --> 04:45.410
-[sniffles]
-Seok-ryu, let's go to the hospital.

04:45.493 --> 04:46.995
-Hye-suk, call your husband.
-Okay.

04:47.078 --> 04:49.038
Tell him we're coming right now, okay?

04:49.122 --> 04:50.415
-[Hye-suk] Okay.
-Mom, I'm fine.

04:50.498 --> 04:51.624
I don't have to go.

04:51.708 --> 04:53.876
What do you mean? Why not?

04:53.960 --> 04:56.838
Seung-hyo, get the car.
We have to go to the hospital now.

04:56.921 --> 04:59.173
No, Mom. I'm fine.

04:59.257 --> 05:01.175
I already had the surgery. I'm okay.

05:03.845 --> 05:06.139
What are you talking about? When?

05:07.348 --> 05:08.808
[voice shaking] Three years ago.

05:09.309 --> 05:13.021
Three years ago?
But that's when you were in the US.

05:14.355 --> 05:15.690
No way.

05:15.773 --> 05:18.359
How could I not know about that?

05:20.945 --> 05:22.030
[Mi-suk's breath trembling]

05:24.741 --> 05:25.825
Is it true?

05:27.035 --> 05:27.952
Really?

05:30.705 --> 05:32.582
[voice shaking] I'm sorry, Mom.
I'm so sorry.

05:38.588 --> 05:39.922
Seung-hyo, did you know?

05:40.006 --> 05:43.051
Did you both lie to me again this time?

05:43.968 --> 05:46.721
[voice shaking] No, I didn't know.
I just found out.

05:46.804 --> 05:47.764
[groans softly]

05:47.847 --> 05:50.349
-[Seok-ryu crying] Mom!
-Mi-suk!

05:51.059 --> 05:52.101
Mi-suk, are you okay?

05:52.185 --> 05:53.811
-Mi-suk.
-[Seok-ryu] Mom!

05:54.312 --> 05:56.564
-[Hye-suk] Where are you going, Mi-suk?
-[Seok-ryu] Mom!

05:56.647 --> 05:57.732
-Mom!
-[Hye-suk] Mi-suk!

06:00.902 --> 06:02.070
[Hye-suk] Seung-hyo.

06:06.783 --> 06:07.700
[Seung-hyo sighs]

06:08.993 --> 06:11.079
-[door opens]
-[both laughing]

06:13.915 --> 06:15.666
Mom! Listen to me!

06:15.750 --> 06:17.085
I can explain everything.

06:17.168 --> 06:18.669
Okay? Mom, please!

06:18.753 --> 06:20.213
-Please, don't.
-[Mi-suk] Honey.

06:21.881 --> 06:24.133
-[Geun-sik] What?
-Honey, she has cancer.

06:25.218 --> 06:26.177
[breathing heavily]

06:27.720 --> 06:28.930
[exhales]

06:29.013 --> 06:30.389
What are you talking about?

06:31.641 --> 06:33.601
Hey, what did your mom say?

06:34.352 --> 06:36.687
[breathing heavily]

06:36.771 --> 06:38.564
She had stomach cancer.

06:40.483 --> 06:42.944
She received surgery
three years ago without telling us.

06:43.027 --> 06:44.904
That's ridiculous.

06:45.613 --> 06:46.697
[breathing heavily]

06:48.741 --> 06:49.659
[exhales]

06:51.244 --> 06:52.286
Seok-ryu.

06:58.084 --> 07:00.211
-It's not true, is it?
-[Seok-ryu sniffles]

07:01.462 --> 07:03.256
[Geun-sik] It's not true, right?

07:03.339 --> 07:06.050
This is… [chuckles nervously] No. No way.

07:06.134 --> 07:07.635
What on earth are you saying?

07:08.427 --> 07:11.347
[Dong-jin] Hey, Seok-ryu.
This is a prank, right?

07:11.430 --> 07:13.724
Why would you joke
about something serious like that?

07:13.808 --> 07:15.101
[Mi-suk groans]

07:15.184 --> 07:16.060
[exhales]

07:16.185 --> 07:19.230
[crying] Mom!

07:21.774 --> 07:22.942
[groans]

07:23.025 --> 07:24.026
[breathing heavily]

07:29.073 --> 07:30.575
[Seok-ryu] Mom!

07:33.119 --> 07:34.203
[exhales]

07:41.002 --> 07:41.836
[inhales]

07:45.882 --> 07:46.716
[Seok-ryu inhales]

07:50.511 --> 07:53.514
[breathing heavily]

07:54.682 --> 07:56.893
Is this why you didn't want to
go to the bathhouse?

07:56.976 --> 07:58.769
Mom, this…

07:59.437 --> 08:00.855
It'll fade.

08:01.564 --> 08:05.318
They said it'll hardly
be noticeable later.

08:05.401 --> 08:06.736
[pills rattling]

08:07.737 --> 08:08.988
What are all these pills?

08:09.822 --> 08:10.823
Why do you have so much?

08:10.907 --> 08:12.617
-Is it because you're sick?
-[Seok-ryu] No.

08:12.700 --> 08:14.285
I'm not sick at all now.

08:14.368 --> 08:16.120
[Mi-suk] Then, why do you have so much?

08:16.204 --> 08:19.165
They're just liver supplements,
probiotics, and vitamins.

08:19.248 --> 08:21.918
Don't leave anything out
and tell me the truth.

08:22.418 --> 08:24.003
What happened to you?

08:24.921 --> 08:25.880
Three years ago,

08:27.048 --> 08:28.799
I had a health checkup in the US.

08:29.550 --> 08:31.886
-And I was diagnosed with stomach cancer.
-[cries]

08:33.513 --> 08:35.848
I had surgery,
and it turned out to be stage 2.

08:37.433 --> 08:39.519
I underwent chemotherapy as a precaution.

08:40.102 --> 08:44.690
But I overcame it.
I'm completely fine now.

08:45.691 --> 08:49.070
Is that why your engagement
was called off? Because you were sick?

08:49.153 --> 08:52.782
-[voice shaking] I'll kill that bastard!
-[Seok-ryu] No, it wasn't like that.

08:53.282 --> 08:55.535
He stayed by my side while I was sick.

08:55.618 --> 08:57.537
He took time off work
and cared for me.

08:57.620 --> 08:58.913
And…

08:59.747 --> 09:02.542
I didn't want to make him suffer anymore.

09:03.167 --> 09:06.963
-So I called the marriage off.
-Do you think parents are a joke?

09:07.588 --> 09:09.173
How…

09:09.257 --> 09:12.635
How could you hide
something like this from us?

09:12.718 --> 09:14.554
I wasn't trying to.

09:15.471 --> 09:17.932
I was going to get treated in the US.

09:18.558 --> 09:21.811
-You'd only worry if you knew.
-Who cares if it was the US?

09:22.395 --> 09:23.437
If their child is sick,

09:23.521 --> 09:26.023
a parent would go
to the moon or Mars for them.

09:27.066 --> 09:30.361
How dare you be so arrogant
and pretend you did this for us?

09:31.320 --> 09:32.321
[voice shaking] Mom.

09:32.405 --> 09:33.239
[Mi-suk] Listen.

09:33.322 --> 09:36.826
You were once a part of me.

09:36.909 --> 09:40.454
While you were in my womb,
you ate the food I ate.

09:40.538 --> 09:42.832
And you drank the water
I drank as you grew.

09:42.915 --> 09:43.874
[sniffles]

09:43.958 --> 09:47.712
I endured 20 hours of labor
before an emergency C-section.

09:47.795 --> 09:49.797
But how could you not tell me
you were sick?

09:49.880 --> 09:52.508
[voice shaking] How? How could I not know?

09:52.592 --> 09:53.801
[sniffles]

09:53.884 --> 09:55.511
I'm sorry, Mom. [crying]

09:56.512 --> 09:57.930
Dad, I'm sorry.

09:59.098 --> 10:00.975
[voice shaking] You should've told us.

10:02.143 --> 10:04.687
You should've told us what was happening.

10:05.521 --> 10:08.357
No matter how useless we are
as your parents…

10:09.150 --> 10:12.153
Still, we should've known.

10:12.236 --> 10:15.072
She thinks she's better than us,
so she doesn't see us as her parents.

10:15.156 --> 10:17.700
No, don't say that. [crying]

10:19.035 --> 10:22.747
I just couldn't tell you.
I couldn't bear to do it.

10:22.830 --> 10:26.083
I wanted to tell you after I got better.

10:26.167 --> 10:29.712
That's what happened.

10:29.795 --> 10:30.838
[sniffles]

10:33.132 --> 10:35.801
I was wrong, Mom. I'm sorry.

10:35.885 --> 10:36.844
[cries]

10:36.927 --> 10:38.304
Goodness.

10:38.387 --> 10:41.432
[whimpering, crying]

10:41.515 --> 10:42.767
[emotional music playing]

10:43.684 --> 10:45.394
-[Dong-jin] Mom.
-[crying]

10:45.478 --> 10:47.521
[footsteps fading]

10:47.605 --> 10:48.439
[sniffles]

10:49.023 --> 10:49.940
Seok-ryu.

10:51.359 --> 10:53.569
[whimpering, sniffles]

10:56.447 --> 10:59.450
[voice shaking] Are you really okay now?

11:00.368 --> 11:01.869
There aren't any problems, right?

11:01.952 --> 11:06.123
Yeah, I'm healthy now. I'm fine.

11:08.167 --> 11:09.543
You don't have to worry.

11:10.127 --> 11:11.837
Okay. [sniffles]

11:12.588 --> 11:13.756
Then, that'll do.

11:13.839 --> 11:15.257
[Seok-ryu groans softly]

11:15.341 --> 11:16.634
That'll do.

11:17.176 --> 11:18.552
[breath trembling]

11:18.636 --> 11:20.596
[breathing heavily]

11:25.393 --> 11:27.812
[breath trembling]

11:33.192 --> 11:34.527
Mom, drink some water.

11:40.074 --> 11:42.743
[breath trembling]

11:46.956 --> 11:48.916
[breathing heavily]

11:48.999 --> 11:51.001
[emotional music continues playing]

11:54.088 --> 11:55.714
-[door closes]
-[sighs]

11:55.798 --> 11:57.466
[breathing heavily]

12:04.765 --> 12:05.766
[sniffles]

12:06.559 --> 12:07.560
[groans softly]

12:09.478 --> 12:11.147
[sniffles, exhales]

12:16.152 --> 12:17.570
[playing drums]

12:27.830 --> 12:29.540
[faint drum sounds]

12:46.974 --> 12:48.809
[faint drum sounds continue]

12:54.690 --> 12:55.691
[exclaims]

13:00.613 --> 13:02.281
[breathing heavily]

13:05.409 --> 13:07.369
[whimpering]

13:07.453 --> 13:09.455
[emotional music continues playing]

13:21.175 --> 13:22.593
[playing drums]

13:27.431 --> 13:29.350
Choisseung was going to
bring me something, so--

13:29.433 --> 13:30.643
[Mi-suk] Talk to him later!

13:30.726 --> 13:33.103
People will talk if they see you here.

13:33.187 --> 13:34.438
Mom.

13:35.606 --> 13:36.899
Are you ashamed of me?

13:36.982 --> 13:39.985
That's right.
I don't even want to see your face.

13:40.069 --> 13:42.154
You're sleeping all day
and fooling around.

13:42.238 --> 13:44.532
Didn't it ever occur to you to wonder

13:44.615 --> 13:46.242
how sleep-deprived I must've been?

13:46.325 --> 13:49.995
Or how little fun I must have had
all these years to fool around like that?

13:50.079 --> 13:52.623
Everyone has it hard. You're not special.

13:52.706 --> 13:54.166
Try having kids of your own.

13:54.792 --> 13:56.627
See if you can treat
your sick child that way.

13:56.710 --> 13:59.880
-Are you taking his side again?
-[objects clattering]

13:59.964 --> 14:01.632
Is being sick that big of a deal?

14:01.715 --> 14:03.676
[continues playing drum]

14:10.933 --> 14:12.226
[sobbing]

14:12.309 --> 14:13.686
[playing drums slowly]

14:22.987 --> 14:23.904
[sniffles]

14:27.116 --> 14:28.284
[groans]

14:29.076 --> 14:31.328
[crying] Why my Seok-ryu?

14:31.412 --> 14:33.622
Why did she have to get cancer?

14:34.623 --> 14:37.042
Why did she have to get sick like that?
[sobbing]

14:37.751 --> 14:39.920
If anyone, it should've been me.

14:40.671 --> 14:44.049
All she ever did was work hard.
She did nothing wrong.

14:44.133 --> 14:46.260
That poor child. [sobbing]

14:53.559 --> 14:55.519
My goodness.

15:06.071 --> 15:07.740
My goodness…

15:09.742 --> 15:12.369
No, my poor girl.

15:13.871 --> 15:15.039
Seok-ryu.

15:15.122 --> 15:16.123
[continues sobbing]

15:21.045 --> 15:24.173
What am I going to do? My poor girl.

15:27.801 --> 15:29.470
[emotional music continues playing]

15:33.307 --> 15:34.683
[knock on door]

15:34.767 --> 15:35.684
[door opens]

15:36.769 --> 15:37.978
[Hye-suk] Seung-hyo.

15:41.190 --> 15:42.399
What's that?

15:43.317 --> 15:44.151
[Hye-suk] Porridge.

15:45.027 --> 15:47.780
You didn't seem well,
so I asked Mi-suk to make it.

15:49.490 --> 15:51.867
I just can't believe what's happened.

15:52.534 --> 15:54.286
Did you come into my room before?

15:54.954 --> 15:55.829
Yeah.

15:59.333 --> 16:01.835
Just leave it here. I'll eat this later.

16:01.919 --> 16:03.587
I heated it. Before it cools, you…

16:04.546 --> 16:05.506
[sighs]

16:05.589 --> 16:06.423
[Hye-suk] Okay.

16:07.424 --> 16:08.592
Rest up.

16:13.097 --> 16:14.932
But did you really not know?

16:15.432 --> 16:18.018
You went to the US
on a business trip three years ago.

16:18.102 --> 16:19.645
You didn't see her then?

16:29.738 --> 16:31.907
-I'm almost there.
-[phone vibrating]

16:31.991 --> 16:33.033
What's this?

16:33.117 --> 16:34.076
MO-EUM

16:34.660 --> 16:36.078
-Hey.
-Hey, Seung-hyo.

16:36.662 --> 16:38.831
-I heard you're in the US.
-How did you know that?

16:38.914 --> 16:40.374
[Mo-eum] Aunt Mi-suk told me.

16:40.457 --> 16:41.542
This is great.

16:41.625 --> 16:43.961
Can you go and see
Seok-ryu while you're there?

16:44.044 --> 16:45.921
She's been so busy I can't reach her.

16:46.005 --> 16:49.299
Hey, do you think I have time to waste?

16:49.383 --> 16:51.385
Don't be like that. Go and see her.

16:52.052 --> 16:53.929
You two are in the same world now.

16:54.013 --> 16:57.224
It's a six-hour plane ride
from New York to California.

16:57.307 --> 17:00.894
I see.
Well, that's practically another country.

17:01.854 --> 17:03.897
I guess they're different worlds.

17:03.981 --> 17:05.482
Got it? Good. Bye.

17:06.483 --> 17:07.443
[line disconnects]

17:16.368 --> 17:17.578
[footsteps approaching]

17:20.581 --> 17:21.457
[inhales]

17:25.586 --> 17:27.087
[slow music playing]

17:35.846 --> 17:36.722
Back then,

17:37.639 --> 17:39.975
I should've run to Seok-ryu.

17:41.769 --> 17:43.353
I should've told her she looked thin

17:44.396 --> 17:46.023
and that she looked tired.

17:47.399 --> 17:49.735
I should've asked her if she was okay.

17:55.365 --> 17:58.243
Could you display the screen in the back?

17:58.327 --> 18:00.412
Please take a look at the documents.

18:00.496 --> 18:03.373
Create new floor plans
to prevent construction errors.

18:03.457 --> 18:05.417
-[man] Okay.
-[phone vibrating]

18:05.501 --> 18:06.376
BAE SEOK-RYU

18:06.460 --> 18:08.337
[lady] Has CAD work
for landscaping started?

18:08.420 --> 18:09.254
[man] Yes.

18:09.338 --> 18:11.548
HEY, YOU'RE IN THE US?
WHY DIDN'T YOU CALL?

18:12.049 --> 18:14.968
Share the bill of quantities
once the working design is complete.

18:15.052 --> 18:17.471
-Any issues with the schedule, right?
-[man] No.

18:17.554 --> 18:21.016
Choi Seung-hyo is a true captain.

18:21.100 --> 18:24.561
You understand? In the sea of life,
we won't get lost with him!

18:24.645 --> 18:26.188
He navigates the way for us.

18:26.271 --> 18:29.566
This is all thanks to him.
Do you all know that?

18:29.650 --> 18:31.652
-You're drunk.
-Hey.

18:31.735 --> 18:33.695
What's that? Who's calling this late?

18:33.779 --> 18:35.781
SEOK-RYU
HOW ARE YOU? YOU MUST BE BUSY

18:35.864 --> 18:37.241
It's nothing.

18:37.741 --> 18:39.243
Hey, you like dried pollock.

18:39.326 --> 18:40.953
[pop song playing]

18:41.036 --> 18:42.371
[mouse clicking]

18:53.841 --> 18:54.883
[phone vibrating]

19:02.808 --> 19:06.854
HAPPY BIRTHDAY, CHOISSEUNG

19:10.065 --> 19:12.401
THANKS

19:18.490 --> 19:19.408
[exhales]

19:22.244 --> 19:23.453
[sighs softly]

19:25.831 --> 19:27.291
[Seung-hyo] But I was a coward,

19:28.417 --> 19:29.835
and while I'd been out of reach,

19:32.421 --> 19:33.589
she was sick.

19:35.591 --> 19:36.842
Without anyone knowing

19:37.885 --> 19:40.095
and alone for a long time.

19:45.684 --> 19:46.894
When I was hurt,

19:46.977 --> 19:48.478
Seok-ryu was the only person

19:49.271 --> 19:51.815
who dragged me out of my cave.

19:53.650 --> 19:54.818
But…

19:55.819 --> 19:58.322
she sent all those signals in the dark,

19:59.072 --> 20:00.115
and I missed them all.

20:03.535 --> 20:08.540
BEAR IN THE CAVE

20:09.917 --> 20:10.918
[birds chirping]

20:16.256 --> 20:17.090
[door opens]

20:17.674 --> 20:18.800
[Mi-suk] What are you doing?

20:19.718 --> 20:20.844
Hey.

20:21.678 --> 20:22.888
Are you making porridge?

20:23.931 --> 20:25.015
[Geun-sik] Yeah.

20:29.728 --> 20:30.854
Take these.

20:31.438 --> 20:32.272
[exclaims softly]

20:32.856 --> 20:34.691
How did you think of freezing these?

20:34.775 --> 20:37.569
It'll upset her
if she sees that our eyes are swollen.

20:38.487 --> 20:39.655
Right.

20:42.991 --> 20:44.660
[Seok-ryu] What are you two doing?

20:44.743 --> 20:45.827
Honey, the porridge.

20:45.911 --> 20:46.912
It's boiling over.

20:46.995 --> 20:49.957
[Geun-sik] Goodness.
I almost wasted all this great porridge.

20:51.333 --> 20:53.126
I'm making abalone porridge.

20:53.210 --> 20:54.419
Because of me?

20:55.462 --> 20:57.130
I don't need to eat porridge.

20:57.714 --> 21:03.345
You should eat food that's easy to digest.
You almost choked on abalone rice before.

21:03.428 --> 21:04.554
[exclaims]

21:04.638 --> 21:07.391
I just had something in my throat then.

21:08.058 --> 21:10.644
I even ate the tteokbokki
you made me last time.

21:11.228 --> 21:12.145
You're right.

21:12.229 --> 21:15.774
Why would you eat that?
You should've said no.

21:15.857 --> 21:17.693
It's good. Why wouldn't I eat it?

21:18.694 --> 21:20.779
Dad, I'm fine. Don't worry.

21:20.862 --> 21:22.155
Still, be careful.

21:22.781 --> 21:25.242
Take me with you
when you visit the doctor next time.

21:25.325 --> 21:27.619
What for? You don't have to come.

21:30.539 --> 21:32.207
Okay, you can come.

21:33.667 --> 21:34.626
Dad, the porridge.

21:34.710 --> 21:38.714
Jeez! I turned down the heat,
but it's still boiling over.

21:41.091 --> 21:43.427
Gosh, I burnt the bottom. [chuckles]

21:44.386 --> 21:45.721
It'll still taste good.

21:46.305 --> 21:47.264
[Jae-suk] Hey.

21:48.432 --> 21:49.599
What do you mean?

21:49.683 --> 21:51.435
Seok-ryu has cancer?

21:51.518 --> 21:54.104
I heard it myself,
but I still don't believe it.

21:54.187 --> 21:56.315
I don't know how this happened.

21:56.398 --> 21:59.401
Hang up. I'm going to call Mi-suk.

21:59.484 --> 22:01.528
Hey, don't.

22:01.611 --> 22:03.905
Just leave her be
until she tells us herself.

22:03.989 --> 22:05.490
Don't act like you know.

22:05.574 --> 22:07.534
How can I do that?

22:07.617 --> 22:11.621
Hey, you might be able to do that,
but I can't!

22:11.705 --> 22:14.541
-I'd rather go and comfort her.
-[door closes]

22:15.584 --> 22:18.211
[voice shaking] Imagine the hard time
she's going through!

22:18.295 --> 22:20.047
Her daughter has cancer.

22:22.049 --> 22:24.926
Mom, what did you just say?

22:30.098 --> 22:31.308
Seok-ryu, you crazy…

22:34.061 --> 22:35.395
[breath trembling]

22:36.063 --> 22:38.148
-How could you hide that?
-Yeah, I hid it.

22:38.231 --> 22:40.275
I didn't tell you. I kept it a secret.

22:40.358 --> 22:41.359
What the hell?

22:41.985 --> 22:44.071
You thought I'd go easy on you
if you confessed?

22:44.154 --> 22:45.238
Don't go easy on me.

22:46.573 --> 22:49.618
What are you doing?
Are you turning yourself in?

22:49.701 --> 22:52.037
I know I deserve to get chewed out.

22:52.120 --> 22:53.997
So do as much as you desire.

22:57.084 --> 22:58.085
No.

22:58.794 --> 23:00.378
I don't do anything that's made easy.

23:00.462 --> 23:04.132
You're not qualified to be a hero.
They love getting things handed to them.

23:04.966 --> 23:05.967
You're right.

23:07.135 --> 23:08.261
I'm not qualified.

23:09.679 --> 23:10.847
I couldn't save you.

23:10.931 --> 23:13.308
Why would you suddenly
say something like that?

23:13.391 --> 23:16.144
A tteokbokki fanatic
suddenly can't eat spicy food.

23:16.812 --> 23:18.313
You drank non-alcoholic beer.

23:19.940 --> 23:22.317
When I think about it,
there were so many clues.

23:23.860 --> 23:25.695
I should've figured it out. Damn it.

23:25.779 --> 23:27.948
Maybe I'm good at acting.

23:28.031 --> 23:30.951
Should I pursue acting instead of cooking?

23:34.955 --> 23:36.081
Did your mom cry a lot?

23:36.164 --> 23:40.043
[sighs] My parents had spoons
on their eyes like this in the morning.

23:40.127 --> 23:41.211
They looked like Ultraman.

23:42.337 --> 23:43.213
I won't cry.

23:45.465 --> 23:46.550
I'll never cry.

23:47.134 --> 23:49.594
If you won't cry or cuss me out,
what will you do?

23:50.178 --> 23:51.054
Well…

23:54.391 --> 23:55.725
I will…

23:59.020 --> 24:00.105
do this.

24:01.815 --> 24:02.983
[slow music playing]

24:03.066 --> 24:05.485
You should've hugged me
like this at the airport.

24:06.903 --> 24:08.071
You're right.

24:10.949 --> 24:12.617
You've endured so much, Seok-ryu.

24:14.327 --> 24:15.537
Physically and mentally.

24:18.206 --> 24:19.624
Thanks.

24:23.086 --> 24:24.588
Just so you know,

24:26.381 --> 24:28.049
you're really flat.

24:29.801 --> 24:31.636
[laughing] I don't feel a thing.

24:31.720 --> 24:34.055
What are you talking about?
We're not even touching!

24:34.139 --> 24:35.974
I'm more curvaceous than you think!

24:36.057 --> 24:37.058
I doubt that.

24:37.142 --> 24:38.185
Want me to get undressed?

24:38.268 --> 24:39.895
-Go ahead.
-I'll really do it.

24:39.978 --> 24:42.439
I meant you're too skinny.

24:44.983 --> 24:47.485
Buy me something nice to eat
if you feel sorry for me.

24:48.862 --> 24:50.864
-I'm paid in peanuts.
-I'm unemployed.

24:51.907 --> 24:54.618
-Should we buy lottery tickets?
-How many?

24:54.701 --> 24:56.578
-How about seven?
-No.

24:56.661 --> 24:59.331
Make it an even number.
It's easier to split.

24:59.915 --> 25:01.291
Okay, let's buy ten!

25:02.042 --> 25:03.168
Sounds good. [chuckles]

25:03.251 --> 25:04.252
[Mo-eum] All right, then.

25:04.336 --> 25:06.213
[both laughing]

25:11.384 --> 25:14.554
Professor, we just had people
from a car accident come in.

25:15.180 --> 25:17.974
The car went up onto the sidewalk
and crashed into a building.

25:18.058 --> 25:19.184
How's are the patients?

25:19.267 --> 25:21.937
The scans show
a pelvic bone fracture in one patient.

25:22.020 --> 25:24.648
One has a clavicle fracture,
and another has a hip fracture.

25:24.731 --> 25:25.857
Let me see.

25:33.156 --> 25:34.282
Bae Seok-ryu?

25:34.366 --> 25:35.408
What?

25:37.077 --> 25:38.078
Oh.

25:38.620 --> 25:40.580
This patient was here a few days ago.

25:41.206 --> 25:43.500
She had surgery
for stomach cancer in the US.

25:43.583 --> 25:45.543
I remembered
because of her unique name.

25:45.627 --> 25:47.128
[solemn music playing]

25:51.675 --> 25:52.634
[sighs]

25:53.635 --> 25:56.137
The client requested a new contractor?

25:56.221 --> 25:57.055
[Myeong-u] Oh.

25:57.138 --> 25:58.181
Why?

25:58.265 --> 26:00.100
He wants to let an acquaintance do it.

26:00.183 --> 26:02.269
The brother-in-law

26:02.352 --> 26:03.603
of his father-in-law's

26:03.687 --> 26:04.980
high school classmate

26:05.063 --> 26:07.607
has a construction firm.

26:07.691 --> 26:09.234
Isn't that a stranger?

26:09.317 --> 26:10.568
Yeah.

26:10.652 --> 26:12.570
But during construction,

26:12.654 --> 26:15.282
the client thinks we could mess with
material and labor costs.

26:15.365 --> 26:17.200
They said they couldn't trust our choice.

26:17.284 --> 26:19.369
[Na-yun] Are they crazy?

26:19.452 --> 26:21.579
Why did they trust us
with the design then?

26:21.705 --> 26:22.998
Switch it for them.

26:23.081 --> 26:24.582
-What?
-What?

26:25.417 --> 26:27.252
We should carry out our client's request.

26:28.795 --> 26:31.089
Get their number, contact them,
and schedule a meeting.

26:31.172 --> 26:34.759
I'll call Mr. Bang
from Sunjong Construction and apologize.

26:34.843 --> 26:37.345
-Yes, sir.
-[Seung-hyo] All right.

26:37.929 --> 26:39.306
Let's wrap up today's meeting.

26:40.557 --> 26:41.975
Keep up the great work.

26:45.478 --> 26:50.233
Wow.
Normally, he would've never allowed this.

26:51.109 --> 26:53.236
He must be in a really good mood today.

26:53.987 --> 26:56.740
No, it's the opposite.

26:57.324 --> 26:59.034
Something's up with him.

27:01.411 --> 27:03.038
I have to ask you something.

27:03.163 --> 27:05.040
Are you free?

27:07.792 --> 27:09.085
[Gyeong-jong] So you knew.

27:11.254 --> 27:14.549
I was debating whether to call you or not.

27:14.632 --> 27:17.385
You know about her condition, right?

27:17.469 --> 27:21.806
Even if you're my son,
I can't release a patient's information.

27:21.890 --> 27:24.559
Can you just tell me if she's okay?

27:26.061 --> 27:27.062
Seung-hyo.

27:28.396 --> 27:30.648
I've always liked Seok-ryu.

27:30.732 --> 27:34.194
A lot of people are awkward with me,
but she never was.

27:35.236 --> 27:38.198
I adored that about her. I was grateful.

27:40.158 --> 27:42.327
Bring Seok-ryu to the hospital.

27:43.578 --> 27:44.913
I'll make sure she's okay.

27:45.997 --> 27:49.167
I promise you.

27:50.001 --> 27:51.836
Okay, Dad.

28:01.179 --> 28:02.138
[both] Mi-suk!

28:02.222 --> 28:04.265
[Jae-suk] Hey, are you okay?

28:04.349 --> 28:06.518
You look so drawn today.

28:06.601 --> 28:09.062
-You didn't get any sleep, did you?
-Mi-suk.

28:09.145 --> 28:11.231
There's an herbal medicine clinic I know.

28:11.314 --> 28:13.316
I asked them what's good
for the stomach.

28:14.067 --> 28:16.361
Cabbages and broccoli.

28:16.444 --> 28:19.197
-And lotus root. Lotus root is great.
-Did you tell them?

28:20.573 --> 28:21.408
Yeah.

28:21.491 --> 28:23.660
Why did you go
and do something I didn't ask for?

28:23.743 --> 28:25.161
It's not like that.

28:25.745 --> 28:28.706
She told us to pretend
like we didn't know.

28:29.332 --> 28:31.292
We're just worried.

28:31.376 --> 28:34.504
Goodness. You even asked them
to act like they didn't know?

28:34.587 --> 28:36.339
Mi-suk, it's not like that.

28:36.423 --> 28:38.758
We just wanted to comfort you.

28:40.427 --> 28:41.928
Why would you comfort me?

28:42.846 --> 28:44.347
Who said I wanted that?

28:44.431 --> 28:46.224
No one asked you to do this!

28:46.808 --> 28:47.892
Na Mi-suk.

28:48.518 --> 28:50.687
You're in one of the five stages of grief.

28:50.770 --> 28:52.439
You're passing through anger.

28:52.522 --> 28:54.524
But that's expected and natural.

28:54.607 --> 28:56.443
You're really something too.

28:56.901 --> 28:59.696
You want to brag
about how smart you are right now?

28:59.779 --> 29:02.407
Fine, just get angry.
Be as angry as you want!

29:02.490 --> 29:04.743
Just take it out on us!

29:05.410 --> 29:06.453
-What?
-You can do that.

29:07.412 --> 29:09.122
We're your friends.

29:09.205 --> 29:10.290
Friends?

29:11.040 --> 29:12.250
So what?

29:12.917 --> 29:15.920
Are friends allowed
to cross the line like this?

29:16.713 --> 29:20.216
Hey, don't talk to me
if you've never experienced it before.

29:20.300 --> 29:22.051
You're right. We haven't.

29:22.135 --> 29:25.138
But we know. Because we're parents too.

29:25.221 --> 29:28.600
We know how you'd rather suffer
in Seok-ryu's place

29:28.683 --> 29:30.769
and how much you blame yourself.

29:30.852 --> 29:32.520
[In-suk crying] Yeah, Mi-suk.

29:32.604 --> 29:35.273
You act tough on the outside,
but we know how sensitive you are.

29:36.441 --> 29:37.901
We know how delicate you are.

29:37.984 --> 29:39.152
[Mi-suk] Goodness.

29:39.736 --> 29:41.196
What am I going to do with Seok-ryu?

29:42.572 --> 29:44.657
[voice shaking] I didn't
even know she was sick.

29:45.784 --> 29:47.327
I'm no mother.

29:47.410 --> 29:50.163
I'm not qualified to be a mother.

29:50.246 --> 29:51.956
My gosh. [sobbing]

29:52.040 --> 29:54.292
-Hey, Mi-suk.
-Mi-suk! [crying]

29:55.293 --> 29:56.795
[all sobbing]

29:56.878 --> 30:00.173
[Hye-suk] No, don't blame yourself.

30:00.256 --> 30:01.424
Okay?

30:01.508 --> 30:03.593
It's okay.

30:03.676 --> 30:07.055
Just cry, you brat. Cry it all out.

30:08.056 --> 30:09.098
[phone vibrating]

30:10.141 --> 30:12.310
SE-HWAN: WHERE ARE YOU?

30:12.393 --> 30:13.311
[insects trilling]

30:13.394 --> 30:16.856
STOMACH CANCER

30:19.484 --> 30:20.777
SURVIVAL RATE RISES TO 78%

30:20.860 --> 30:22.403
EARLY DETECTION AND PREVENTION ARE KEY

30:32.163 --> 30:33.456
[groans]

30:34.415 --> 30:35.625
Bae Seok-ryu.

30:36.543 --> 30:38.419
She looks strong enough to eat rocks.

30:38.920 --> 30:40.046
How could she get sick?

30:42.257 --> 30:44.342
-Damn it.
-[Na-yun exclaiming]

30:44.425 --> 30:45.844
[Dong-jin] Are you okay?

30:45.927 --> 30:48.930
No, I'm not okay. I almost got hurt.

30:49.681 --> 30:51.516
-You're our gym member.
-[Na-yun] What?

30:51.599 --> 30:52.684
What are you doing here?

30:53.893 --> 30:55.770
-Shouldn't you be at work?
-[Dong-jin] Oh.

30:56.813 --> 30:57.772
I quit.

30:58.356 --> 31:01.109
That place wasn't big enough
for someone like me.

31:01.192 --> 31:03.194
I see. So you were fired.

31:03.278 --> 31:04.904
No, I wasn't!

31:04.988 --> 31:06.489
I left on my own.

31:06.573 --> 31:09.033
You were about to be fired,
so you quit first.

31:09.117 --> 31:09.993
No, I didn't!

31:11.119 --> 31:14.873
Take this advice from someone who's had
more experience in the workplace.

31:14.956 --> 31:18.001
Get on your knees
and beg for your job back.

31:18.084 --> 31:19.002
Why would I?

31:19.711 --> 31:21.546
You don't know anything.
Why are you meddling?

31:21.629 --> 31:22.964
Meddling?

31:24.132 --> 31:26.050
That's not something I ever do.

31:27.927 --> 31:31.514
I'm just giving you advice
after what you did with the treadmill.

31:31.598 --> 31:32.640
[pleasant music playing]

31:32.724 --> 31:35.685
I was running too fast back then.

31:41.566 --> 31:44.068
Hey, your strides are too long!

31:44.152 --> 31:45.194
[Na-yun] I can't hear you.

31:45.278 --> 31:47.530
The optimal cadence
for running is 180 bpm.

31:47.614 --> 31:49.407
So what cadence is…

31:49.490 --> 31:50.867
I think you hear me.

31:50.950 --> 31:52.076
[Na-yun] Jeez.

31:58.124 --> 31:58.958
Ms. Jung.

32:03.671 --> 32:04.589
Ms. Jung?

32:05.715 --> 32:06.966
[exclaims]

32:07.050 --> 32:08.426
[both grunt]

32:08.509 --> 32:09.886
[Mo-eum exclaiming]

32:09.969 --> 32:10.970
[dog barks distantly]

32:12.597 --> 32:14.515
-[Dan-ho exclaiming in pain]
-[Mo-eum sobbing]

32:15.266 --> 32:17.226
-[coughs]
-[Mo-eum continues sobbing]

32:18.645 --> 32:19.854
[weakly] Ms. Jung.

32:26.277 --> 32:27.946
[Mo-eum] Slowly.

32:28.029 --> 32:29.948
[mellow music playing]

32:30.031 --> 32:31.699
-Be careful when you sit.
-Okay.

32:33.952 --> 32:35.161
[Mo-eum grunts softly]

32:35.244 --> 32:36.329
[Dan-ho exhales]

32:36.412 --> 32:37.372
[Mo-eum] Are you okay?

32:38.873 --> 32:42.043
Let's just go to the hospital.
I think you need an X-ray.

32:42.126 --> 32:43.628
It's fine.

32:44.087 --> 32:46.589
Who knew I'd end up
feeling the power of a black belt?

32:46.673 --> 32:47.548
[chuckles softly]

32:48.466 --> 32:51.678
You should've known how to avoid it
if you were a red belt.

32:51.761 --> 32:52.762
[chuckles softly]

32:52.845 --> 32:54.472
Do you have pain relief patches?

32:54.555 --> 32:55.848
[Dan-ho] Um…

32:56.557 --> 32:59.227
-No.
-Wait here. I'll go buy some.

33:01.062 --> 33:04.857
It's fine, so just sit for a second.

33:08.778 --> 33:10.989
[Mo-eum] Maybe I have some at my house.

33:11.656 --> 33:12.991
I'm really okay.

33:14.033 --> 33:16.452
I'm not that weak.

33:20.581 --> 33:22.250
I didn't say anything.

33:26.963 --> 33:27.797
[exhales]

33:30.425 --> 33:34.053
Can I ask why you were crying back there?

33:34.137 --> 33:38.016
Why are you asking to ask
when you've already done so?

33:39.434 --> 33:41.185
-You're right.
-[chuckles softly]

33:43.521 --> 33:44.480
The thing is…

33:45.231 --> 33:48.651
this is actually a very popular place
for listening to people's problems.

33:49.318 --> 33:51.195
I've already had someone here before.

33:52.947 --> 33:55.033
Who? Choi Seung-hyo?

33:56.868 --> 33:57.785
Oh.

33:57.869 --> 33:59.328
How did you know?

34:00.079 --> 34:03.666
Well, the security maintenance here
seemed like a mess.

34:07.003 --> 34:08.004
Oh.

34:10.006 --> 34:11.758
[scoffs] No wonder.

34:14.969 --> 34:16.220
You see,

34:17.346 --> 34:20.433
it's about a friend of mine, not me.

34:21.684 --> 34:24.395
My friend has a really close friend.

34:25.980 --> 34:28.524
They've been best friends
since they were kids.

34:29.942 --> 34:32.028
That friend lived abroad for a long time.

34:32.820 --> 34:33.905
I see.

34:34.739 --> 34:36.032
[Mo-eum] But…

34:36.115 --> 34:37.992
my friend's friend…

34:39.077 --> 34:40.078
Um…

34:42.789 --> 34:44.040
had surgery…

34:46.876 --> 34:49.087
for cancer three years ago.

34:51.923 --> 34:52.799
And my friend

34:53.841 --> 34:55.843
just found out recently.

34:57.887 --> 35:01.516
Your friend must be having
a really hard time.

35:02.100 --> 35:03.226
But…

35:05.228 --> 35:07.855
she keeps acting
like she's not having a hard time.

35:08.648 --> 35:10.024
[slow music playing]

35:11.442 --> 35:13.486
But it's killing me.

35:17.990 --> 35:18.825
[gasps]

35:19.826 --> 35:22.036
I mean, I'm not talking about me.

35:23.037 --> 35:25.998
It's my friend. And my friend's friend.

35:26.707 --> 35:28.292
Why is this so confusing?

35:28.376 --> 35:31.087
It's not about me.
It's my friend's friend.

35:32.046 --> 35:33.381
Don't worry.

35:33.464 --> 35:35.925
I'll make sure
security is tighter this time.

35:41.305 --> 35:42.223
[groans softly]

35:45.434 --> 35:46.561
Well…

35:48.729 --> 35:50.857
I can't believe Seok-ryu's sick.

35:53.526 --> 35:55.361
Due to the nature of my job,

35:56.487 --> 35:58.823
I see a lot of sick people.

36:00.658 --> 36:02.410
And people on the verge of death.

36:04.120 --> 36:05.288
But…

36:09.041 --> 36:12.420
[voice shaking] …I never imagined that
Seok-ryu could be one of those people.

36:13.045 --> 36:13.963
[sniffles]

36:14.046 --> 36:16.966
I said I wouldn't cry, but I can't stop.

36:19.677 --> 36:20.887
You can cry here.

36:22.388 --> 36:23.389
What?

36:24.098 --> 36:26.142
Cry a little bit here in secret.

36:26.225 --> 36:27.810
Then, smile even more after that.

36:29.562 --> 36:31.439
Share a drink with her.

36:32.023 --> 36:35.610
Chat, have fun, and just be with her.

36:36.444 --> 36:37.278
[sniffles]

36:37.361 --> 36:40.281
Being with someone
who miraculously returned

36:41.574 --> 36:44.035
is a miracle in itself.

36:44.118 --> 36:45.620
[slow music continues playing]

36:45.703 --> 36:48.456
It's just like what Yeon-du means to me.

36:50.291 --> 36:52.126
-Yeon-du?
-[Dan-ho] Yes.

36:54.670 --> 36:56.214
It was two years ago.

36:57.882 --> 37:00.343
I looked at my phone
after finishing an interview.

37:01.052 --> 37:04.180
I'd several missed calls
from the same number.

37:05.181 --> 37:07.391
I called back and they said

37:08.517 --> 37:09.727
it was the hospital.

37:12.104 --> 37:13.356
[panting]

37:30.373 --> 37:31.415
[man] Is this her?

37:35.836 --> 37:37.964
[inhales, breath trembling]

37:38.047 --> 37:39.966
[breathing heavily]

37:45.263 --> 37:46.430
[breath trembling]

37:52.603 --> 37:53.562
My child.

37:55.690 --> 37:57.108
[voice shaking] I have a child.

37:59.986 --> 38:01.320
Where is she?

38:06.993 --> 38:09.078
KANG YEON-DU
DO HYEON-WOO

38:09.161 --> 38:11.414
IN SURGERY

38:11.497 --> 38:13.040
[slow music continues playing]

38:17.044 --> 38:18.087
[sniffles]

38:20.589 --> 38:21.757
Yeon-du…

38:22.800 --> 38:25.553
miraculously survived the accident
and came back to me.

38:26.929 --> 38:27.930
[Mo-eum] Dan-ho…

38:28.556 --> 38:34.145
So I know how precious
each ordinary morning is.

38:35.855 --> 38:37.815
Waking her up every morning,

38:39.025 --> 38:41.235
feeding her breakfast,

38:41.736 --> 38:43.321
running to daycare together

38:44.196 --> 38:45.990
so she's not late,

38:47.825 --> 38:50.244
and seeing her wave goodbye to me

38:52.204 --> 38:53.539
as she walks inside.

38:53.622 --> 38:54.999
Ordinary days like that.

38:56.250 --> 38:57.710
So you should also…

39:01.422 --> 39:03.090
You said it was okay to cry.

39:06.594 --> 39:07.928
Why are you holding it in?

39:09.472 --> 39:11.223
[mellow music playing]

39:13.726 --> 39:15.603
I'll keep it secret too.

39:54.308 --> 39:55.476
[Dan-ho grunting]

39:56.644 --> 39:57.978
[quirky music playing]

40:05.611 --> 40:06.612
[mutters]

40:07.655 --> 40:09.115
[panting]

40:11.075 --> 40:12.201
[breathing heavily]

40:14.286 --> 40:16.872
What's the point of running away?
I live next door.

40:19.125 --> 40:20.084
[door closes]

40:33.431 --> 40:34.348
[music ends]

40:34.849 --> 40:36.892
[jazz music playing in the background]

40:46.652 --> 40:48.070
[Hye-suk] Sorry.

40:48.154 --> 40:51.615
I forgot we were supposed to
have lunch together.

40:51.699 --> 40:52.950
That's okay.

40:53.701 --> 40:55.494
We can just have dinner together.

40:55.995 --> 40:57.121
I must be getting old.

40:57.204 --> 40:59.457
I've never made such mistakes before.

40:59.540 --> 41:01.000
What? It's cute.

41:02.126 --> 41:03.127
[Hye-suk] Thank you.

41:03.210 --> 41:05.629
Seo Hye-suk's doing things
unlike her usual self.

41:05.713 --> 41:07.590
My gosh. What's this?

41:07.673 --> 41:09.717
Chablis wine. Nice, right?

41:09.800 --> 41:11.635
It's so nice.

41:11.719 --> 41:12.928
As for me,

41:13.012 --> 41:16.390
I'm used to hearing adjectives
like "beautiful" and "cool."

41:16.474 --> 41:18.726
But "cute"? That's not bad either.

41:18.809 --> 41:20.311
[both chuckle]

41:23.522 --> 41:24.523
Cheers.

41:29.361 --> 41:30.446
Mmm.

41:30.988 --> 41:32.281
This really is nice.

41:33.449 --> 41:36.118
What did you need to discuss with me?

41:36.202 --> 41:37.203
Well…

41:41.373 --> 41:44.710
Have you thought about my offer?

41:45.711 --> 41:46.712
I see.

41:50.758 --> 41:51.759
That?

41:56.472 --> 41:57.598
[Hye-suk] What's this?

41:59.016 --> 42:00.851
Why did you come here?

42:01.519 --> 42:02.978
Well…

42:03.062 --> 42:04.188
I had something to tell you.

42:10.069 --> 42:12.321
What do you mean? Take time off?

42:13.322 --> 42:16.283
It's how it sounds.
You've been overdoing things.

42:16.867 --> 42:18.035
[scoffs]

42:18.118 --> 42:20.621
I didn't overdo things. I just worked.

42:21.455 --> 42:22.581
Right.

42:23.666 --> 42:26.377
"The Woman of the Wind
who crossed the Sahara Desert."

42:26.460 --> 42:28.295
"The Foreign Ministry's African Tongue."

42:28.379 --> 42:31.715
Jeez. Go get everyone
who gave me those names.

42:31.799 --> 42:33.676
-I'll teach them.
-[chuckles]

42:34.718 --> 42:36.762
You've lived up to your names

42:37.596 --> 42:39.932
by being in the field
for over 20 years now.

42:41.350 --> 42:42.977
Let's take a break.

42:43.936 --> 42:46.814
Let's eat and have tea at our leisure.

42:54.572 --> 42:56.824
I know that you're worried.

42:57.950 --> 43:01.662
But I want to stay on active duty.
I'm years away from retirement too.

43:03.122 --> 43:06.542
I'll speak to the minister myself
and ask him where I should go.

43:06.625 --> 43:07.543
You…

43:09.336 --> 43:10.254
can't go anywhere.

43:11.547 --> 43:12.381
What?

43:12.464 --> 43:13.299
Because…

43:14.633 --> 43:15.843
you won't be reassigned.

43:16.427 --> 43:17.553
Oh. [chuckles]

43:18.554 --> 43:20.723
I bet there aren't
any suitable positions right now.

43:20.806 --> 43:22.016
I'll wait then.

43:22.099 --> 43:23.642
It doesn't matter which country it is.

43:23.726 --> 43:26.562
-When a spot opens, anywhere is--
-There's no point in waiting.

43:28.522 --> 43:30.566
You understand what I mean, right?

43:31.525 --> 43:34.820
You're telling me to just collect my pay
while on standby with no job?

43:37.323 --> 43:39.491
-Don't tell me…
-You'll hear soon.

43:40.492 --> 43:42.202
You'll be asked to voluntarily resign.

43:43.704 --> 43:44.663
[scoffs]

43:45.497 --> 43:46.707
Did you agree with it too?

43:49.168 --> 43:50.544
It was an organizational decision.

44:03.140 --> 44:04.183
Sure.

44:08.020 --> 44:09.605
Then, I'll have to accept it.

44:34.421 --> 44:35.339
[sighs softly]

44:39.593 --> 44:40.886
You're mad at me, right?

44:42.429 --> 44:43.263
No.

44:44.223 --> 44:45.683
Then, why didn't you call me?

44:47.935 --> 44:49.186
I was busy.

44:49.269 --> 44:51.647
Liar. You were avoiding me.

44:54.900 --> 44:57.528
I know. It's because of my cancer.

44:58.821 --> 45:00.489
It bothers you to look at me.

45:02.116 --> 45:04.993
You don't know if you need to
comfort me or encourage me.

45:06.245 --> 45:08.163
You probably don't know what to say.

45:09.456 --> 45:11.500
Hey, it's like that at my house too.

45:11.583 --> 45:13.836
My mom's crying.
My dad's having a hard time.

45:14.795 --> 45:18.424
Even Dong-jin's become pale with fear.

45:19.007 --> 45:22.261
They walk on eggshells around me.
It's so uncomfortable.

45:22.886 --> 45:24.930
I knew this would happen.

45:25.013 --> 45:27.599
That's why I kept it a secret.

45:28.517 --> 45:31.061
But no one understands
how thoughtful I was being.

45:31.895 --> 45:33.147
Yeah, right.

45:34.022 --> 45:37.651
Seok-ryu, you're saying
you kept this a secret for our sake?

45:39.570 --> 45:42.990
No, you only thought about yourself.

45:48.620 --> 45:50.998
You're a coward, and you're pathetic.

45:51.707 --> 45:53.083
What?

45:53.167 --> 45:55.836
You're weak and hypocritical.

45:55.919 --> 45:57.129
Hey.

45:57.212 --> 45:58.213
You…

45:59.923 --> 46:02.551
hurt the people who love you.

46:04.928 --> 46:06.805
You did the unthinkable.

46:06.889 --> 46:08.015
[slow music playing]

46:08.098 --> 46:10.350
To your mom, your dad, me.

46:11.477 --> 46:12.811
And to yourself.

46:14.771 --> 46:15.772
You…

46:16.899 --> 46:19.067
in your loneliest
and most difficult moment,

46:19.943 --> 46:21.195
left yourself alone.

46:23.280 --> 46:24.114
Seok-ryu.

46:26.325 --> 46:27.784
When things are really tough,

46:29.286 --> 46:31.205
you lean on the people closest to you.

46:31.288 --> 46:32.664
What if I did lean on them?

46:35.000 --> 46:36.376
Would that have changed anything?

46:38.253 --> 46:40.631
If I'm hurting,
you'd all be hurting with me.

46:42.508 --> 46:45.219
If I fall, you'd fall with me
like dominoes.

46:45.302 --> 46:48.430
Who cares if we fall?
Who cares if things crumble?

46:49.056 --> 46:50.390
We can hit rock bottom together.

46:50.474 --> 46:52.059
Then, we can get back up again.

46:52.142 --> 46:54.061
I don't know how to do that.

46:54.144 --> 46:56.021
This is who I am,
so what can I do?

46:56.104 --> 46:57.731
You did it for me!

46:59.358 --> 47:01.276
When my mom left for Africa

47:01.944 --> 47:04.363
and when I had to quit swimming
because I hurt my leg,

47:05.155 --> 47:06.782
you reached out to me.

47:06.865 --> 47:08.242
You stayed with me.

47:08.325 --> 47:09.284
Hey.

47:10.202 --> 47:11.203
That's…

47:12.120 --> 47:13.413
That's different.

47:13.497 --> 47:15.749
But why won't you give me
the chance to do the same?

47:16.917 --> 47:18.627
You did all those things for me.

47:20.295 --> 47:22.464
Why won't you let me do the same for you?

47:23.465 --> 47:24.466
That's enough.

47:26.760 --> 47:27.594
Let's stop.

47:28.637 --> 47:31.473
Seok-ryu. Are you running away again?

47:32.724 --> 47:33.892
Stop!

47:34.851 --> 47:36.186
I said stop!

47:38.689 --> 47:39.523
[sighs]

47:58.792 --> 48:00.836
I should've done the same back then.

48:01.670 --> 48:03.088
Just like you,

48:03.171 --> 48:05.090
I should've shouted and gotten angry.

48:05.924 --> 48:07.384
I should've been more honest.

48:09.636 --> 48:10.929
Back then,

48:11.597 --> 48:12.514
was Seok-ryu…

48:15.517 --> 48:16.935
in a lot of pain?

48:18.604 --> 48:22.190
She endured it courageously.

48:23.942 --> 48:24.901
[sighs]

48:39.583 --> 48:40.500
[exclaims]

48:43.128 --> 48:43.962
[groans]

48:44.630 --> 48:45.631
[Geun-sik exclaims]

48:46.256 --> 48:47.090
[sighs]

48:48.050 --> 48:50.302
I thought the alcohol
would be sweet, but it's bitter.

48:50.385 --> 48:51.720
[liquid pouring]

48:51.803 --> 48:52.763
[exhales]

48:53.263 --> 48:54.222
That's good.

48:55.307 --> 48:56.600
We can split this bottle

48:57.309 --> 48:58.852
and go to bed.

49:02.272 --> 49:03.482
[both sigh]

49:05.484 --> 49:06.443
Honey.

49:07.527 --> 49:08.487
[exhales]

49:08.570 --> 49:11.365
I keep thinking about all the wrong things
I've done to Seok-ryu.

49:12.991 --> 49:14.743
When Seok-ryu was three,

49:15.869 --> 49:17.537
Dong-jin was crying at night.

49:20.332 --> 49:22.250
She woke up and started to cry too.

49:24.002 --> 49:25.712
So I scolded her.

49:28.131 --> 49:30.467
I said, "You're a big kid.
Why are you crying?"

49:31.259 --> 49:33.261
"Why are you giving me a hard time too?"

49:34.638 --> 49:35.889
You were young.

49:37.557 --> 49:38.850
You didn't know.

49:39.893 --> 49:41.186
Still…

49:43.188 --> 49:44.731
I shouldn't have done that.

49:47.150 --> 49:48.985
I think I made this happen to her.

49:52.406 --> 49:54.533
My excuse was I had to
give Dong-jin extra care,

49:56.451 --> 49:58.370
and I pushed her too much to the side.

49:59.371 --> 50:00.247
But…

50:01.123 --> 50:04.167
she grew up so well on her own.

50:05.043 --> 50:06.253
Yeah, she did.

50:08.171 --> 50:09.089
Our daughter…

50:09.923 --> 50:12.426
never caused us any trouble. [inhales]

50:13.593 --> 50:17.180
[voice shaking] That poor girl
must've tried so hard to do that.

50:17.264 --> 50:18.724
She must've been so stressed.

50:18.807 --> 50:19.808
[both whimpering]

50:21.101 --> 50:23.311
But all I did
was boast about it to others.

50:23.395 --> 50:25.981
I never gave her
the support she needed. [sniffles]

50:27.065 --> 50:30.694
She was so worried
that she endured such an awful thing…

50:30.777 --> 50:33.071
[sniffles] …all on her own. [sobbing]

50:36.575 --> 50:38.118
[voice shaking] It's mostly my fault.

50:39.995 --> 50:41.037
[breath trembling]

50:41.121 --> 50:44.875
Gosh, that restaurant was doomed anyway.
Why did I try so hard?

50:44.958 --> 50:46.376
[slow music playing]

50:47.669 --> 50:49.921
I wasn't able to focus
on my family. [sniffles]

50:50.922 --> 50:52.758
I passed it off onto you.

50:53.341 --> 50:54.634
[sobbing, sniffles]

50:54.718 --> 50:58.555
I feel terrible for what I did to her.
What am I going to do? [sobbing]

51:00.891 --> 51:01.725
I'm so sorry.

51:02.684 --> 51:04.728
I'm sorry.

51:07.189 --> 51:09.065
I'm sorry to you. [sniffles]

51:11.151 --> 51:12.819
And I'm sorry to Seok-ryu.

51:15.447 --> 51:16.782
Honey, what do we do? [sobbing]

51:19.534 --> 51:20.869
[Geun-sik whimpering]

51:22.788 --> 51:24.039
[both whimpering]

51:26.208 --> 51:28.168
[Mi-suk sobbing] I'm so sorry.

51:29.294 --> 51:31.505
[Geun-sik] I'm sorry. [sobbing]

51:31.588 --> 51:32.422
I'm so…

51:36.676 --> 51:38.011
[voice shaking] I'm sorry.

51:41.389 --> 51:43.767
[Mi-suk sobbing] Honey,
what are we going to do?

51:45.393 --> 51:46.478
[music ends]

51:48.230 --> 51:49.356
[birds chirping]

51:53.568 --> 51:54.444
[exhales]

51:55.153 --> 51:56.029
[door closes]

51:56.112 --> 51:57.322
[amusing music playing]

52:12.379 --> 52:15.715
I can't even greet Yeon-du
because of my careless lips.

52:17.509 --> 52:21.263
All of this happened
because I had a lot on my mind.

52:21.346 --> 52:24.558
As a result, it short-circuited a little.

52:25.517 --> 52:26.977
Let's put out the fire.

52:27.477 --> 52:28.770
I have to extinguish it.

52:28.854 --> 52:30.230
[breathes deeply]

52:35.068 --> 52:36.486
Why did she hide?

52:39.322 --> 52:40.490
Is she playing hide-and-seek?

52:41.283 --> 52:45.036
-What are you talking about?
-Mo-eum just hid after she saw us.

52:45.120 --> 52:46.371
I saw her.

52:48.623 --> 52:51.334
We're late. Yeon-du, should we run?

52:51.918 --> 52:53.461
-Yeah.
-[Dan-ho] Ready, set, go!

52:53.545 --> 52:54.880
[Yeon-du] I'm going to beat you!

52:55.922 --> 52:57.591
[Yeon-du talking indistinctly]

52:58.884 --> 53:00.260
Hey, Seok-ryu.

53:07.517 --> 53:08.476
Seok-ryu?

53:12.272 --> 53:14.149
She left her phone. Where did she go?

53:14.941 --> 53:16.109
[phone vibrating]

53:23.533 --> 53:26.828
JEONGHEON UNIVERSITY HOSPITAL
BAE SEOK-RYU, YOUR BIOPSY RESULTS ARE OUT

53:26.912 --> 53:27.913
[exhales]

53:27.996 --> 53:29.414
[slow music playing]

53:32.459 --> 53:33.501
[indistinct conversation]

53:43.595 --> 53:44.554
[Seung-hyo] Back then,

53:45.889 --> 53:46.848
was Seok-ryu…

53:47.557 --> 53:49.267
in a lot of pain?

53:50.185 --> 53:53.688
She endured it courageously.

53:54.439 --> 53:55.315
[sighs]

53:59.778 --> 54:00.987
At least,

54:03.323 --> 54:04.783
that's what I thought.

54:04.866 --> 54:06.785
[slow music continues playing]

54:06.868 --> 54:08.495
After her surgery,

54:09.371 --> 54:10.580
about a year passed…

54:13.124 --> 54:14.542
and she developed depression.

54:17.879 --> 54:19.297
Depression?

54:20.507 --> 54:21.716
I didn't know.

54:25.971 --> 54:27.889
She was falling apart alone.

54:29.182 --> 54:30.100
[metal bangs]

54:31.518 --> 54:32.978
[supervisor] Be careful!

54:33.061 --> 54:33.895
[employee] Yes, sir!

54:33.979 --> 54:35.230
Please be careful.

54:36.773 --> 54:38.650
Mr. Choi, could you come here?

54:38.733 --> 54:40.402
Can you explain this?

54:40.485 --> 54:41.403
[Seung-hyo] Sure.

54:43.571 --> 54:44.948
[Myeong-u] Here.

54:45.031 --> 54:47.534
So this isn't your average structure.

54:47.617 --> 54:49.703
I thought it'd be hard to implement.

54:50.328 --> 54:53.999
I'll send you a detailed floor plan
and additional materials to explain.

54:54.082 --> 54:56.209
We'd be grateful for that.

54:56.292 --> 54:58.211
As for that area, if you look here…

54:58.294 --> 54:59.379
[phone vibrating]

54:59.462 --> 55:00.755
Just a moment. Sorry.

55:04.009 --> 55:05.093
Hi, Aunt Mi-suk.

55:06.594 --> 55:08.596
What? Seok-ryu?

55:09.431 --> 55:10.724
[mellow music playing]

55:11.057 --> 55:12.267
[indistinct chatter]

55:13.601 --> 55:14.602
[sighs softly]

55:15.603 --> 55:17.022
[doorbell chiming]

55:24.154 --> 55:24.988
[exhales]

55:28.575 --> 55:29.993
[panting]

55:32.579 --> 55:33.496
[exhales]

55:37.709 --> 55:38.877
HYEREUNG COOKING SCHOOL

55:39.753 --> 55:41.046
[panting]

55:50.388 --> 55:51.306
[panting]

55:59.147 --> 55:59.981
[exhales]

56:09.199 --> 56:10.658
[mellow music continues playing]

56:23.338 --> 56:24.297
[tires screech]

56:36.810 --> 56:37.685
Seriously?

56:45.735 --> 56:46.569
[music ends]

56:46.653 --> 56:47.695
Hey, Seok-ryu!

56:49.906 --> 56:50.740
Choisseung?

56:51.783 --> 56:53.034
What are you doing?

56:53.118 --> 56:54.327
How did you know I was here?

56:54.410 --> 56:58.081
If you're going to go somewhere,
you should let people know!

56:58.164 --> 56:59.999
How could you disappear
without your phone?

57:00.083 --> 57:01.835
Well, that…

57:01.918 --> 57:04.295
interferes with my deep meditation
and self-reflection--

57:04.379 --> 57:06.005
[Seung-hyo] Are you joking?

57:06.089 --> 57:08.466
Do you know how much
I've been looking for you?

57:08.550 --> 57:10.468
Do you know how worried everyone is?

57:10.552 --> 57:13.596
I came here
because I was frustrated, okay?

57:13.680 --> 57:15.098
I need to breathe too.

57:15.181 --> 57:16.307
Hey.

57:16.391 --> 57:19.060
Because of you,
I'm the one who's suffocating here.

57:19.144 --> 57:21.271
How long were you
going to keep it a secret?

57:21.354 --> 57:22.939
How long were you
going to hide it for?

57:23.022 --> 57:26.025
You want to talk about this again?
Aren't you sick of it already?

57:26.109 --> 57:28.528
Your emotional pain,
not your physical pain.

57:30.321 --> 57:31.156
You…

57:33.575 --> 57:34.868
had depression.

57:35.618 --> 57:36.786
Why didn't you tell me?

57:37.704 --> 57:38.955
Where did you hear that?

57:41.124 --> 57:42.542
Did you see Hyeon-jun?

57:42.625 --> 57:44.294
Seriously, what's wrong with you?

57:46.212 --> 57:47.589
Are you a fool?

57:47.672 --> 57:49.299
Why are you so stupid?

57:49.382 --> 57:52.010
How much have you bottled up
in that tiny body of yours?

57:52.093 --> 57:53.136
Stop it. I'm leaving.

57:53.219 --> 57:54.345
[sighs]

57:55.430 --> 57:56.806
[Seok-ryu exclaims] Hey!

57:56.890 --> 57:58.892
What are you doing?

57:58.975 --> 58:00.518
What on earth are you doing?

58:00.602 --> 58:01.561
Hey!

58:01.644 --> 58:04.022
Wait! What are you doing?

58:04.105 --> 58:05.231
[waves splashing]

58:05.315 --> 58:06.483
[Seok-ryu screams]

58:07.734 --> 58:08.943
Hey, what are you doing?

58:09.027 --> 58:10.236
Are you insane?

58:10.320 --> 58:11.654
[screaming]

58:11.738 --> 58:13.364
[mellow music playing]

58:18.912 --> 58:20.872
What are you doing, you lunatic?

58:20.955 --> 58:23.291
You said you were frustrated.
Isn't it refreshing now?

58:23.374 --> 58:24.250
Hey!

58:24.334 --> 58:26.794
[Seung-hyo] Yeah.
You should shout like that.

58:26.878 --> 58:27.712
[pop song playing]

58:27.795 --> 58:29.339
You have everything pent up inside.

58:30.298 --> 58:31.466
Let it all out.

58:32.634 --> 58:36.095
What's inside you is bitterness.

58:36.179 --> 58:37.055
So…

58:39.182 --> 58:41.976
don't try to foolishly
carry that burden alone!

58:42.685 --> 58:43.937
Let it all out here.

58:45.730 --> 58:47.482
Why are you yelling at me?

58:49.150 --> 58:50.652
Why do you keep getting angry at me?

58:51.778 --> 58:53.738
I'm the one who was sick.

58:54.656 --> 58:56.449
I'm the one who's having the hardest time.

58:56.533 --> 58:59.160
[voice shaking] Why do you
keep scolding me?

59:01.371 --> 59:02.872
I wasn't being angry at you.

59:05.124 --> 59:06.334
I'm mad at myself.

59:09.254 --> 59:11.422
After I heard you were sick,
I thought back.

59:14.092 --> 59:15.385
I didn't hear you…

59:16.719 --> 59:17.804
knocking on my door.

59:22.433 --> 59:24.185
You sent me signs
that you were struggling.

59:25.603 --> 59:27.438
But I had my eyes and ears closed.

59:32.569 --> 59:34.571
Even though I knew that…

59:36.573 --> 59:38.283
I said those harsh things to you.

59:41.744 --> 59:45.290
I felt so pathetic and frustrated.
I felt like garbage.

59:50.878 --> 59:52.505
Why didn't you text me back?

59:54.173 --> 59:55.341
I'm sorry.

59:56.718 --> 59:58.428
Why did you ignore my calls?

01:00:00.221 --> 01:00:01.055
I'm sorry.

01:00:04.309 --> 01:00:05.143
[crying]

01:00:05.226 --> 01:00:09.522
I wasn't able to tell anyone!

01:00:09.606 --> 01:00:11.566
Do you know how scared I was on my own?

01:00:14.736 --> 01:00:17.280
Why did you do that?

01:00:19.324 --> 01:00:24.454
I was so worried my parents
would collapse from shock if I told them!

01:00:24.996 --> 01:00:27.874
I had all sorts of thoughts
in my head when I made this decision.

01:00:27.957 --> 01:00:32.086
I debated if I should tell you or not
over a hundred times. [sobbing]

01:00:34.005 --> 01:00:36.049
You don't know anything!

01:00:36.132 --> 01:00:38.217
You don't know how I feel!

01:00:58.237 --> 01:00:59.322
[continues crying]

01:01:01.908 --> 01:01:03.159
[waves splashing]

01:01:20.718 --> 01:01:21.761
Here.

01:01:22.470 --> 01:01:24.555
Nothing beats banana milk
after going for a swim.

01:01:24.639 --> 01:01:25.640
[chuckles softly]

01:01:26.974 --> 01:01:29.310
It's nice. It's like when we'd visit
the bathhouse as kids.

01:01:29.977 --> 01:01:30.853
[Seung-hyo exhales]

01:01:37.110 --> 01:01:37.944
[Seok-ryu] Mmm.

01:01:39.320 --> 01:01:42.156
Hey, you haven't answered me yet.

01:01:43.574 --> 01:01:44.992
How did you know I was here?

01:01:45.993 --> 01:01:47.870
This is where you ran away to before.

01:01:48.621 --> 01:01:49.956
It was short-lived though.

01:01:50.039 --> 01:01:51.874
You didn't have to say that part.

01:01:52.375 --> 01:01:54.168
It's true that I ran away.

01:01:55.211 --> 01:01:57.213
It was justified too.

01:01:58.256 --> 01:01:59.590
Mom.

01:01:59.674 --> 01:02:01.551
How come only he gets a new phone?

01:02:02.135 --> 01:02:05.471
How come only Dong-jin
gets a new phone?

01:02:05.555 --> 01:02:08.307
Gosh, I had no choice. His was broken.

01:02:08.391 --> 01:02:11.060
Mine's broken too. It broke twice.

01:02:11.144 --> 01:02:12.729
But I had it fixed!

01:02:12.812 --> 01:02:15.356
I said I'd buy you one
if you got the highest mock exam score.

01:02:15.898 --> 01:02:17.191
-But you didn't.
-[coughing]

01:02:17.275 --> 01:02:19.986
He's the dumbest kid in school,
but you bought him one!

01:02:20.069 --> 01:02:21.487
This takes great pictures.

01:02:21.571 --> 01:02:23.906
-They're killer!
-Delete them or I'll kill you.

01:02:23.990 --> 01:02:26.075
-[Mi-suk] Seung-hyo, are you okay?
-Yeah.

01:02:26.159 --> 01:02:28.244
[Mi-suk] Look, you think I wanted
to buy him one?

01:02:28.327 --> 01:02:30.455
I can't reach this brat without a phone!

01:02:30.538 --> 01:02:33.249
Also, all gadgets are the same.

01:02:33.332 --> 01:02:34.709
Try to be more like Seung-hyo.

01:02:34.792 --> 01:02:37.503
He's been using the same phone for years.

01:02:37.587 --> 01:02:39.213
But he's never complained once.

01:02:39.297 --> 01:02:41.007
-What a sweet boy.
-[Seok-ryu] Mom, listen.

01:02:41.591 --> 01:02:43.593
Only his phone is old.

01:02:43.676 --> 01:02:45.470
Everything else he owns is expensive.

01:02:45.553 --> 01:02:47.096
-[groans]
-Look at this. This shirt?

01:02:47.180 --> 01:02:49.557
-Let go. Get your hands off me.
-It's over 100,000 won!

01:02:49.640 --> 01:02:51.684
And he only wears
foreign-brand underwear. Look!

01:02:51.768 --> 01:02:52.602
What are you doing?

01:02:52.685 --> 01:02:54.187
-[Mi-suk] Stop!
-Are you crazy?

01:02:54.270 --> 01:02:55.813
This is so unfair, Mom.

01:02:55.897 --> 01:02:58.566
How come only he gets
a swivel phone and not me?

01:02:58.649 --> 01:03:01.194
[voice shaking] You always let
stuff like this happen!

01:03:01.277 --> 01:03:02.278
It's not fair!

01:03:02.361 --> 01:03:03.613
[pleasant music playing]

01:03:04.781 --> 01:03:06.824
[waves splashing]

01:03:07.575 --> 01:03:09.327
Jeez, what is wrong with her?

01:03:12.288 --> 01:03:15.833
I want to go back!

01:03:17.877 --> 01:03:19.587
You wore your uniform to school,

01:03:19.670 --> 01:03:22.215
went to all your classes,
and then ran away.

01:03:22.840 --> 01:03:24.342
Does that even count?

01:03:25.510 --> 01:03:27.637
Absences would lower your grades.

01:03:29.722 --> 01:03:31.057
Fine, forget it.

01:03:31.140 --> 01:03:33.184
I didn't have much guts.

01:03:34.185 --> 01:03:35.353
It's because you're too nice.

01:03:35.436 --> 01:03:36.854
[pleasant music continues playing]

01:03:36.938 --> 01:03:38.022
What?

01:03:38.105 --> 01:03:40.149
You were mad
and felt things were unfair,

01:03:40.983 --> 01:03:43.611
but you didn't want to worry your parents.

01:03:43.694 --> 01:03:45.238
So that was your compromise.

01:03:46.614 --> 01:03:48.825
My brother was always causing problems.

01:03:50.618 --> 01:03:54.455
But I was the one
who caused the biggest mess.

01:03:58.376 --> 01:03:59.418
[slurping]

01:04:00.253 --> 01:04:01.379
I'm done.

01:04:04.048 --> 01:04:05.341
[sighs audibly]

01:04:05.424 --> 01:04:09.136
I'd wish for nothing more
than a cold beer to chug right now.

01:04:12.974 --> 01:04:14.392
But I can't do that anymore.

01:04:15.643 --> 01:04:16.686
That makes me sad.

01:04:23.860 --> 01:04:24.735
Make the call.

01:04:25.486 --> 01:04:26.320
To who?

01:04:26.404 --> 01:04:27.530
My dad.

01:04:28.531 --> 01:04:30.241
They said you got a text
from the hospital.

01:04:31.284 --> 01:04:32.702
Your biopsy results are out.

01:04:34.245 --> 01:04:37.665
That? Later. I can do that later.

01:04:37.748 --> 01:04:39.750
Not later. Do it now while I'm here.

01:04:42.044 --> 01:04:45.923
Do you remember when they put
seven metal pins in my leg?

01:04:46.507 --> 01:04:48.801
Yeah. Why?

01:04:48.885 --> 01:04:52.805
Did something happen when you stubbed
your foot into the bed that time?

01:04:52.889 --> 01:04:55.057
What? No.

01:04:57.727 --> 01:05:00.479
But once you injure a knee,
it can get hurt again.

01:05:01.814 --> 01:05:04.984
If that happens, I'm going to
take you with me to the hospital.

01:05:05.651 --> 01:05:06.986
Don't I get any say in it?

01:05:07.069 --> 01:05:10.114
I'm going to make you buy me juice.

01:05:10.197 --> 01:05:13.326
And what else? I'll make you
get comic books for me.

01:05:13.868 --> 01:05:16.495
-And I'll ask you to wash my greasy hair.
-[scoffs]

01:05:16.579 --> 01:05:17.872
That's ridiculous.

01:05:17.955 --> 01:05:18.956
Who says I'll do it?

01:05:19.040 --> 01:05:20.124
I'd do it for you.

01:05:22.376 --> 01:05:24.503
That's what I'm going to do
no matter what you say.

01:05:27.465 --> 01:05:28.549
So…

01:05:29.050 --> 01:05:31.302
don't worry that something might happen.

01:05:33.596 --> 01:05:36.724
Call them,
and I'll stay by your side.

01:05:41.145 --> 01:05:42.313
[slow music playing]

01:05:46.275 --> 01:05:47.234
[Seok-ryu sighs]

01:05:47.318 --> 01:05:50.488
FATHER

01:05:51.989 --> 01:05:53.324
[line ringing]

01:05:57.119 --> 01:05:59.497
Hello, sir. It's Seok-ryu.

01:06:00.790 --> 01:06:01.749
Yes.

01:06:03.709 --> 01:06:05.211
I'm sorry I hid it from you.

01:06:07.213 --> 01:06:08.047
So…

01:06:08.839 --> 01:06:11.217
I heard the biopsy results are out.

01:06:14.387 --> 01:06:15.346
Right.

01:06:17.515 --> 01:06:18.349
Okay.

01:06:20.810 --> 01:06:21.644
Oh.

01:06:22.353 --> 01:06:23.354
Okay, I understand.

01:06:24.772 --> 01:06:25.606
Okay, bye.

01:06:30.987 --> 01:06:32.196
What did he say?

01:06:32.822 --> 01:06:34.448
He said it was nothing.

01:06:34.532 --> 01:06:36.450
It was just an infection. I'm clean.

01:06:36.534 --> 01:06:37.702
[sighs deeply]

01:06:37.785 --> 01:06:39.578
[pleasant music playing]

01:06:39.662 --> 01:06:40.579
[exhales]

01:06:45.626 --> 01:06:49.463
-Hey, why the hell are you hugging me?
-Just…

01:06:50.756 --> 01:06:52.383
Let me give you a damn hug.

01:06:55.136 --> 01:06:56.721
[sighs deeply]

01:07:18.367 --> 01:07:19.493
Goodness.

01:07:24.582 --> 01:07:26.751
Gosh.

01:07:27.960 --> 01:07:28.961
[sighs wearily]

01:07:38.763 --> 01:07:40.514
[pleasant music continues playing]

01:08:06.248 --> 01:08:08.000
-[clears throat]
-[line ringing]

01:08:12.004 --> 01:08:13.881
Where are you right now?

01:08:17.927 --> 01:08:19.553
Professor, are you going to eat?

01:08:19.637 --> 01:08:20.471
Yeah.

01:08:20.554 --> 01:08:22.807
The cafeteria's serving bibimbap today.

01:08:22.890 --> 01:08:24.391
I'm going to have steak.

01:08:24.475 --> 01:08:25.893
What? They're serving steak?

01:08:25.976 --> 01:08:27.561
Professor, where…

01:08:27.645 --> 01:08:28.896
The cafeteria's this way.

01:08:29.772 --> 01:08:30.856
Professor?

01:08:32.858 --> 01:08:33.859
[music ends]

01:08:46.080 --> 01:08:47.414
[dramatic music playing]

01:08:48.249 --> 01:08:50.668
[female 1] It's the vice minister
and ambassador.

01:08:51.418 --> 01:08:55.089
-[female 1] Didn't they graduate together?
-[female 2] Yeah, they're really close.

01:08:55.172 --> 01:08:57.383
They went to Africa together
in the past too.

01:08:58.467 --> 01:08:59.927
What's with the flowers?

01:09:01.053 --> 01:09:04.306
[female 3] Who knows?
There are tons of rumors about them.

01:09:04.390 --> 01:09:08.269
It's well-known. They say
the vice minister isn't married yet

01:09:08.352 --> 01:09:10.771
because the ambassador still is.

01:09:10.855 --> 01:09:12.481
[female 1 gasps] That's insane.

01:09:20.948 --> 01:09:21.824
[music ends]

01:09:28.497 --> 01:09:31.458
Hey, Mo-eum did the same thing too.

01:09:31.542 --> 01:09:33.919
Why are you expressing
your friendship with hugs now?

01:09:34.837 --> 01:09:35.880
Not me.

01:09:37.006 --> 01:09:38.883
I told you we're not friends anymore.

01:09:43.554 --> 01:09:46.056
We're here.
It's so quick without the traffic.

01:09:52.688 --> 01:09:54.648
Where are we going? That was my house.

01:09:56.775 --> 01:09:59.737
Wait, where are we going?
Hello? Where are we going?

01:10:00.446 --> 01:10:02.156
My legs are falling asleep.

01:10:02.907 --> 01:10:03.741
-Mom.
-Yeah?

01:10:03.824 --> 01:10:05.201
Do we have to do all this?

01:10:05.284 --> 01:10:06.452
I know from experience,

01:10:06.535 --> 01:10:08.579
but a surprise party requires patience.

01:10:08.662 --> 01:10:10.873
-Hang in there.
-When is Seok-ryu coming?

01:10:10.956 --> 01:10:12.374
The food's getting cold.

01:10:12.458 --> 01:10:13.292
-Aunt Mi-suk.
-Yeah?

01:10:13.375 --> 01:10:15.711
-This cake didn't come with any matches.
-[Geun-sik] Huh?

01:10:16.420 --> 01:10:17.338
That can't be.

01:10:17.421 --> 01:10:19.840
Does anyone have a lighter?

01:10:20.716 --> 01:10:22.593
I may drink, but I don't smoke.

01:10:23.427 --> 01:10:25.262
Should I start smoking again then?

01:10:26.222 --> 01:10:28.349
How can you not have
lighters in a kitchen?

01:10:28.432 --> 01:10:29.808
Well, yeah. It's a kitchen.

01:10:30.434 --> 01:10:31.894
I have a torch. Hold on.

01:10:31.977 --> 01:10:33.437
-I'll shine a light.
-Where was it?

01:10:33.520 --> 01:10:35.356
-Help him find it.
-It's so dark. I can't see.

01:10:35.439 --> 01:10:36.357
My legs.

01:10:37.233 --> 01:10:39.151
[Seung-hyo] Hey, wait. Slow down.

01:10:39.276 --> 01:10:40.903
-[Seok-ryu] For what?
-[Seung-hyo] Okay?

01:10:40.986 --> 01:10:41.904
[Seung-hyo] Hey.

01:10:41.987 --> 01:10:43.530
[Mi-suk] It works.

01:10:43.614 --> 01:10:45.074
-The door's unlocked.
-Slow down.

01:10:46.700 --> 01:10:48.285
[amusing music playing]

01:10:49.370 --> 01:10:51.580
CONGRATULATIONS
SEOK-RYU'S WELCOME HOME PARTY

01:10:55.376 --> 01:10:56.210
[Seok-ryu] My gosh!

01:10:57.044 --> 01:10:59.588
-Surprise!
-Surprise!

01:10:59.672 --> 01:11:01.131
[all cheering]

01:11:03.008 --> 01:11:06.220
Mom, Dad? What's going on?

01:11:07.513 --> 01:11:08.764
Well, so…

01:11:09.348 --> 01:11:11.892
We wanted to throw a party
to welcome you back home.

01:11:11.976 --> 01:11:16.272
[laughs] But I've been home
for some time now.

01:11:16.855 --> 01:11:19.775
This is so cheesy. Whose idea was this?

01:11:19.858 --> 01:11:21.527
It was him.

01:11:21.610 --> 01:11:22.444
Him.

01:11:23.862 --> 01:11:25.781
[Seok-ryu] This is ridiculous.

01:11:25.864 --> 01:11:27.241
[Geun-sik] What will you do?

01:11:27.324 --> 01:11:29.118
[line ringing]

01:11:29.201 --> 01:11:31.495
Aunt Mi-suk, I found Seok-ryu.

01:11:32.288 --> 01:11:34.999
Yeah. But I was thinking.

01:11:35.082 --> 01:11:37.584
How about we give her
a welcome home party tonight?

01:11:38.168 --> 01:11:39.461
I know it's a little late,

01:11:39.545 --> 01:11:42.214
but we didn't do anything for her
when she came home.

01:11:42.798 --> 01:11:44.341
What are you doing?

01:11:44.425 --> 01:11:47.052
I mean, I just… [clears throat]

01:11:47.136 --> 01:11:48.887
I just wanted to
have a meal with everyone.

01:11:49.888 --> 01:11:51.557
You prepared a lot, Uncle Geun-sik.

01:11:51.640 --> 01:11:54.351
-Because you told me to.
-Okay, then!

01:11:54.435 --> 01:11:55.936
-Come in.
-Let's sit, everyone.

01:11:56.020 --> 01:11:58.439
-Sit down.
-Yeah, let's sit.

01:11:58.522 --> 01:11:59.898
Goodness!

01:11:59.982 --> 01:12:03.777
Chef, please introduce tonight's dishes.

01:12:03.861 --> 01:12:06.238
[all cheering]

01:12:06.322 --> 01:12:08.699
-What's with you all? [laughs]
-[all laughing]

01:12:08.782 --> 01:12:12.453
It's been a while for me.
I'm a little nervous. [laughs]

01:12:12.536 --> 01:12:14.538
Wait a second. All right.

01:12:14.621 --> 01:12:17.166
Tonight's main dish is

01:12:17.249 --> 01:12:21.170
gungjung tteokbokki, which was served
originally during the Joseon Dynasty.

01:12:21.253 --> 01:12:24.923
It has rice cakes made with
organic brown rice fresh from the mill.

01:12:25.007 --> 01:12:28.469
They've been cooked and reduced
in the chef's special sauce

01:12:28.552 --> 01:12:31.013
for the person I love the most
in the whole world…

01:12:31.472 --> 01:12:32.306
[sniffles]

01:12:36.018 --> 01:12:37.144
For my daughter,

01:12:40.647 --> 01:12:42.775
I present this special dish. [chuckles]

01:12:42.858 --> 01:12:45.027
-[Dong-jin] A round of applause!
-[all clapping]

01:12:46.028 --> 01:12:46.987
Thanks, Dad.

01:12:47.571 --> 01:12:51.241
This is the only type of tteokbokki
you can eat now. Got it?

01:12:51.325 --> 01:12:53.202
Okay.

01:12:53.952 --> 01:12:56.705
Weren't you worried the food
would get cold? What a long speech.

01:12:56.789 --> 01:12:57.956
-Let's eat.
-Goodness!

01:12:58.040 --> 01:12:59.583
You should say a few words too.

01:12:59.666 --> 01:13:00.709
-[Dong-jin] Yeah.
-Hey! No.

01:13:00.793 --> 01:13:02.836
-A speech to welcome her home.
-Hurry up.

01:13:02.920 --> 01:13:05.381
-I'll do it sitting down.
-[laughs]

01:13:07.800 --> 01:13:09.009
We're a family.

01:13:09.093 --> 01:13:10.260
[pleasant music playing]

01:13:10.344 --> 01:13:12.513
A family doesn't just share
the good times.

01:13:13.472 --> 01:13:17.893
A family shares the difficult, sad,
and painful times together too.

01:13:20.687 --> 01:13:21.730
So…

01:13:23.148 --> 01:13:24.191
from now on,

01:13:25.109 --> 01:13:26.902
no more keeping things to yourself.

01:13:27.486 --> 01:13:28.695
[Dong-jin] No more.

01:13:28.779 --> 01:13:31.073
That's our family motto now.

01:13:31.949 --> 01:13:33.409
-Our motto!
-Sounds good!

01:13:34.284 --> 01:13:35.452
Friends are family too!

01:13:36.537 --> 01:13:38.622
-Family!
-Just join our family. [laughs]

01:13:39.498 --> 01:13:41.834
We have so many kids.
We have four of them.

01:13:41.917 --> 01:13:43.585
We've always been family.

01:13:43.669 --> 01:13:45.254
That's right.

01:13:45.337 --> 01:13:46.296
[Mo-eum] Yeah. Hey.

01:13:46.380 --> 01:13:48.924
But what do we do about the cake?
We didn't light it.

01:13:49.007 --> 01:13:50.968
It's fine. Our surprise failed.
Don't do it.

01:13:51.051 --> 01:13:53.345
No, we can have it for dessert later.

01:13:53.429 --> 01:13:55.055
-[Mo-eum] Yeah, okay.
-[Geun-sik] Okay.

01:13:56.890 --> 01:13:59.893
This is fried yam.
Yams are good for the stomach.

01:13:59.977 --> 01:14:02.855
I'm going to grate and fry them
for your breakfast and dinner.

01:14:02.938 --> 01:14:05.023
-You better eat them all.
-[Dong-jin] Hey.

01:14:05.107 --> 01:14:06.275
Eat up.

01:14:06.358 --> 01:14:08.235
How dare you talk that way
your older sister?

01:14:08.318 --> 01:14:09.153
You brat!

01:14:09.236 --> 01:14:11.029
-Her name's not "Hey."
-Be respectful.

01:14:11.113 --> 01:14:12.030
[Mi-suk] Do it now.

01:14:13.574 --> 01:14:15.701
Seok-ryu, eat up.

01:14:15.784 --> 01:14:18.328
-[Mo-eum exclaims]
-[Geun-sik chuckles]

01:14:19.872 --> 01:14:21.623
-[Seok-ryu] Let's eat!
-Thanks for the food!

01:14:21.707 --> 01:14:22.791
Thank you for the meal.

01:14:23.625 --> 01:14:25.502
[indistinct chatter, laughter]

01:14:30.632 --> 01:14:31.508
[music ends]

01:14:34.344 --> 01:14:35.220
[Mo-eum grunts]

01:14:35.304 --> 01:14:37.598
-I'm so full.
-[laughs]

01:14:37.681 --> 01:14:39.057
My stomach might explode.

01:14:39.600 --> 01:14:40.809
[dog barks distantly]

01:14:45.272 --> 01:14:46.899
-What?
-[Geun-sik] What?

01:14:46.982 --> 01:14:48.525
No, it's not what I meant.

01:14:48.609 --> 01:14:50.819
That's how good the food was.
I ate a lot.

01:14:50.903 --> 01:14:52.488
That's what I meant.

01:14:53.655 --> 01:14:57.451
Seriously, I'm okay. Don't worry.

01:14:57.534 --> 01:14:58.952
-You scared us.
-[Dong-jin sighs]

01:14:59.786 --> 01:15:01.997
-[Mo-eum] She says she's fine.
-All right.

01:15:02.080 --> 01:15:03.999
Come up to the rooftop tomorrow.

01:15:04.082 --> 01:15:05.375
I'll be your personal trainer.

01:15:05.459 --> 01:15:08.629
Are you insane?
Why would I entrust my body to you?

01:15:08.712 --> 01:15:09.630
I'll help you too.

01:15:09.713 --> 01:15:12.299
-Honorary paramedic, Bae Seok-ryu.
-So cheesy!

01:15:12.382 --> 01:15:14.384
-Gross.
-[Mo-eum] Hey, call 119.

01:15:14.468 --> 01:15:17.804
I'll come faster than anyone
from the dispatch center.

01:15:17.888 --> 01:15:20.766
[chuckles softly] I love
getting this type of treatment.

01:15:20.849 --> 01:15:23.101
My dad's going to
make me gungjung tteokbokki.

01:15:23.185 --> 01:15:24.686
That's not all.

01:15:24.770 --> 01:15:27.397
I'll make you whatever you want,
three square meals a day.

01:15:27.481 --> 01:15:30.025
-Of course.
-Then, what about you?

01:15:30.108 --> 01:15:31.235
Will you build me a house?

01:15:31.318 --> 01:15:32.945
[scoffs] Don't get your hopes up.

01:15:33.028 --> 01:15:34.530
-That sounds good.
-Seung-hyo.

01:15:34.613 --> 01:15:35.864
It was worth a try.

01:15:35.948 --> 01:15:37.533
-Aunt Mi-suk!
-What about you, Mom?

01:15:37.616 --> 01:15:41.036
I'll scrub your back.
Let's go to the bathhouse tomorrow.

01:15:41.620 --> 01:15:42.579
Okay, let's go.

01:15:42.663 --> 01:15:44.289
[Geun-sik chuckles]

01:15:44.373 --> 01:15:46.708
Want to come too? Just like old times?

01:15:47.292 --> 01:15:50.170
Why would I go with you?
You lunatic. Don't be ridiculous.

01:15:50.254 --> 01:15:53.131
I mean, we can just go
to the bathhouse together.

01:15:53.215 --> 01:15:55.467
Then, we'll part ways
in front of the lockers.

01:15:55.551 --> 01:15:57.261
-What were you thinking?
-[Mi-suk] Yeah.

01:15:57.344 --> 01:15:59.429
[Seung-hyo] I wasn't thinking
about anything. Jeez.

01:15:59.513 --> 01:16:01.223
[Mo-eum] He's stuttering.
He was thinking.

01:16:01.306 --> 01:16:03.183
-[Seok-ryu] He's flustered.
-[Mo-eum] He did!

01:16:03.308 --> 01:16:05.477
[Mi-suk] Hey, stop ganging up
on Seung-hyo!

01:16:05.561 --> 01:16:06.687
-You did? Why you…
-I didn't!

01:16:06.770 --> 01:16:08.730
-[Geun-sik] Come here!
-[Seung-hyo] I'm innocent!

01:16:08.814 --> 01:16:10.482
Why is he going in?

01:16:11.191 --> 01:16:12.985
[Geun-sik] You better have
that house built!

01:16:13.068 --> 01:16:14.570
[indistinct chatter, laughter]

01:16:14.653 --> 01:16:16.363
[slow music playing]

01:16:19.241 --> 01:16:20.075
[music ends]

01:16:20.158 --> 01:16:21.076
[door opens]

01:16:24.371 --> 01:16:25.455
[door closes]

01:16:27.291 --> 01:16:28.417
[Hye-suk] You're home late.

01:16:39.261 --> 01:16:42.014
I'm sorry. I couldn't make it to lunch.

01:16:42.097 --> 01:16:45.142
No, it's fine.

01:16:46.893 --> 01:16:49.062
Things were hectic for me too,
so I forgot.

01:16:51.273 --> 01:16:52.190
Honey.

01:16:54.109 --> 01:16:55.652
I have something to tell you.

01:17:01.325 --> 01:17:02.159
[sighs]

01:17:04.286 --> 01:17:05.412
So do I.

01:17:05.495 --> 01:17:08.540
Go ahead. Mine might take a while.

01:17:10.042 --> 01:17:11.668
Let's get a divorce.

01:17:15.631 --> 01:17:16.632
What?

01:17:16.715 --> 01:17:17.758
I want a divorce.

01:17:24.139 --> 01:17:25.140
[phone vibrating]

01:17:25.223 --> 01:17:28.769
HYEON-JUN

01:17:32.939 --> 01:17:33.899
[exhales]

01:17:36.276 --> 01:17:37.319
Hello?

01:17:38.070 --> 01:17:39.112
[Hyeon-jun] You picked up.

01:17:40.739 --> 01:17:41.990
I'm glad.

01:17:42.074 --> 01:17:43.617
I have no reason not to.

01:17:45.285 --> 01:17:46.203
Where are you?

01:17:46.286 --> 01:17:48.413
Where else? I'm at my hotel.

01:17:49.498 --> 01:17:51.583
[Seok-ryu] Did you have something to say?

01:17:52.250 --> 01:17:53.126
Yeah.

01:17:55.837 --> 01:17:57.297
I'm going back to the US.

01:17:59.383 --> 01:18:00.425
I think…

01:18:02.177 --> 01:18:04.054
this call might be

01:18:04.721 --> 01:18:06.431
the last one I give you.

01:18:06.515 --> 01:18:07.933
[slow music playing]

01:18:10.936 --> 01:18:11.978
Seok-ryu.

01:18:14.356 --> 01:18:15.357
I…

01:18:17.401 --> 01:18:19.111
loved you so much.

01:18:21.655 --> 01:18:22.656
But…

01:18:24.074 --> 01:18:24.908
[sighs]

01:18:26.952 --> 01:18:29.329
…I think the way I loved you was wrong.

01:18:31.039 --> 01:18:33.709
I only focused on
getting you back on your feet.

01:18:35.293 --> 01:18:37.754
I never thought to fall down with you.

01:18:39.715 --> 01:18:41.591
It was only after I came to Korea…

01:18:44.511 --> 01:18:47.222
that I realized who the people
you truly needed were…

01:18:49.641 --> 01:18:52.060
and where you needed to be.

01:18:54.187 --> 01:18:55.188
I'm sorry.

01:18:56.273 --> 01:18:57.232
Back then,

01:18:58.734 --> 01:19:00.819
I couldn't relate to your pain.

01:19:02.028 --> 01:19:03.405
I couldn't accept you…

01:19:05.574 --> 01:19:07.367
for who you were.

01:19:08.118 --> 01:19:09.453
No, it was my fault.

01:19:10.454 --> 01:19:11.997
I used being sick as an excuse

01:19:13.623 --> 01:19:15.292
and exploited you.

01:19:17.043 --> 01:19:18.754
I was so consumed with my own emotions

01:19:21.131 --> 01:19:22.382
that I didn't recognize…

01:19:25.010 --> 01:19:26.386
how lonely you were.

01:19:27.596 --> 01:19:30.724
Seok-ryu,

01:19:32.642 --> 01:19:34.478
let's not regret the time we shared.

01:19:36.313 --> 01:19:39.441
Let's remember
how I was everything to you

01:19:41.443 --> 01:19:43.987
and how you meant
everything to me back then.

01:19:46.698 --> 01:19:48.074
That should be enough then.

01:19:50.410 --> 01:19:51.495
Okay.

01:19:53.497 --> 01:19:54.581
All right.

01:19:58.502 --> 01:19:59.336
Take care.

01:20:01.338 --> 01:20:02.672
You too.

01:20:07.427 --> 01:20:08.386
[line disconnects]

01:20:10.514 --> 01:20:11.348
[sighs]

01:20:16.061 --> 01:20:17.646
[slow music continues playing]

01:20:23.109 --> 01:20:25.946
[sighs deeply]

01:20:38.208 --> 01:20:39.167
[music ends]

01:20:39.251 --> 01:20:40.418
[birds chirping]

01:20:47.717 --> 01:20:48.802
[door opens]

01:20:49.302 --> 01:20:50.428
Hi.

01:20:51.137 --> 01:20:52.264
Are you going to work?

01:20:52.722 --> 01:20:54.057
Are you going to class?

01:20:54.140 --> 01:20:56.017
I asked you first.

01:20:56.643 --> 01:20:59.104
What, you think
I'd be getting off work at this hour?

01:21:00.063 --> 01:21:03.900
True. Hey, don't work too late.

01:21:03.984 --> 01:21:06.152
It's pointless to devote yourself to work.

01:21:06.736 --> 01:21:08.697
It's my company. I'll take care of it.

01:21:09.322 --> 01:21:10.615
That's true too.

01:21:10.699 --> 01:21:14.411
All right, you take care of it,
and have a great day.

01:21:14.494 --> 01:21:15.704
[amusing music playing]

01:21:15.787 --> 01:21:16.621
You too.

01:21:18.373 --> 01:21:19.916
Hey, why are you following me?

01:21:20.000 --> 01:21:22.335
[Seung-hyo] I'm not.
I said I'm going to work.

01:21:22.419 --> 01:21:25.005
Yeah, I know that. But go a different way.

01:21:25.088 --> 01:21:28.383
Before I cook, I need time
to seriously meditate alone.

01:21:30.176 --> 01:21:31.261
[dog barking]

01:21:33.555 --> 01:21:34.973
Hey, you're following me.

01:21:38.435 --> 01:21:39.394
What are you doing?

01:21:40.729 --> 01:21:42.022
-Hyeong-chan.
-Yes, sir?

01:21:42.105 --> 01:21:43.231
[Seung-hyo] Come here.

01:21:44.274 --> 01:21:46.318
Why is the proposal so flat?

01:21:46.401 --> 01:21:48.236
Did you finish analyzing
the surrounding area?

01:21:48.320 --> 01:21:50.572
-What about the commercial district?
-Not yet.

01:21:50.655 --> 01:21:53.074
After we prepare
the construction procedures first--

01:21:53.158 --> 01:21:54.993
You did things in the wrong order.

01:21:55.076 --> 01:21:58.496
If we review regulations and build
according to those sizes, we're done?

01:21:58.580 --> 01:21:59.497
[pop song playing]

01:21:59.581 --> 01:22:03.460
You need to work
with the brand in mind from the start.

01:22:03.543 --> 01:22:05.712
If we only consider the ratios,

01:22:05.795 --> 01:22:07.589
why would the clients come to us?

01:22:08.673 --> 01:22:11.051
[Hyeong-chan] I'm sorry.
I'll have it redone.

01:22:12.177 --> 01:22:15.889
I don't think
Mr. Choi's in a good mood today.

01:22:15.972 --> 01:22:16.973
-No…
-[Seung-hyo] Na-yun.

01:22:17.057 --> 01:22:17.933
Yes?

01:22:18.016 --> 01:22:20.977
Did you review Misom's flagship store
and its environmental sustainability?

01:22:21.061 --> 01:22:22.938
No, not yet.

01:22:23.021 --> 01:22:25.523
I asked you to do that a while ago.
You still haven't finished?

01:22:25.607 --> 01:22:26.775
I'm sorry.

01:22:26.858 --> 01:22:28.151
-Speed it up.
-[Na-yun] Yes, sir.

01:22:30.862 --> 01:22:32.906
He's in a great mood today.

01:22:32.989 --> 01:22:33.823
[door closes]

01:22:33.907 --> 01:22:35.283
He's super happy.

01:22:41.581 --> 01:22:43.500
[Seung-hyo] It can bear fruit?

01:22:44.292 --> 01:22:45.377
Can it bloom flowers too?

01:22:45.460 --> 01:22:46.419
Of course.

01:22:47.754 --> 01:22:50.006
Our friend has a lot to do this year.

01:22:50.632 --> 01:22:51.675
Then…

01:22:52.175 --> 01:22:54.552
What should I do to listen to my tree?

01:22:55.971 --> 01:22:59.265
[shop owner] First off,
it needs a lot of sunshine

01:22:59.349 --> 01:23:02.477
for around six to ten hours a day.

01:23:02.560 --> 01:23:06.606
Also, it likes warm temperatures.

01:23:07.482 --> 01:23:10.568
Putting it in a place with a good breeze
will make it feel less humid.

01:23:11.903 --> 01:23:13.738
Don't be withering alone again.

01:23:15.198 --> 01:23:16.950
Tell me if you have something to say.

01:23:17.951 --> 01:23:18.910
I promise…

01:23:20.203 --> 01:23:21.621
I'll listen carefully.

01:23:22.872 --> 01:23:25.709
POMEGRANATE TREE

01:23:26.710 --> 01:23:27.711
[song ends]

01:23:28.586 --> 01:23:29.713
[phone vibrating]

01:23:36.052 --> 01:23:36.928
[inhales]

01:23:37.554 --> 01:23:38.430
[chuckles softly]

01:23:40.015 --> 01:23:40.849
Get up now.

01:23:40.932 --> 01:23:42.350
[Seok-ryu] What? What is it?

01:23:42.434 --> 01:23:44.561
-[Seung-hyo] We have to go somewhere.
-Where?

01:23:44.644 --> 01:23:47.147
-[Seung-hyo] There's no time. Get up.
-I can't go like this!

01:23:47.272 --> 01:23:48.732
-It's fine.
-You're in a suit.

01:23:48.815 --> 01:23:50.108
-What?
-I didn't wash my hair!

01:23:50.191 --> 01:23:51.109
You don't have to.

01:23:51.192 --> 01:23:54.070
-You lunatic, where are we going?
-[Seung-hyo] There's no time.

01:23:56.322 --> 01:23:57.532
Hey.

01:23:58.241 --> 01:23:59.784
-Come on.
-Why are we here?

01:23:59.868 --> 01:24:01.119
[indistinct announcement]

01:24:06.833 --> 01:24:08.251
Why are we here?

01:24:08.960 --> 01:24:10.211
Song Hyeon-jun.

01:24:13.631 --> 01:24:14.591
Choisseung.

01:24:15.091 --> 01:24:16.718
[mellow music playing]

01:24:16.801 --> 01:24:19.345
Wait here. I'm first.

01:24:26.352 --> 01:24:28.855
Don't tell me you're here to see me off.

01:24:29.397 --> 01:24:30.356
With Seok-ryu?

01:24:30.440 --> 01:24:32.776
Isn't this why you messaged me?

01:24:36.154 --> 01:24:37.363
This is Song Hyeon-jun.

01:24:38.031 --> 01:24:40.241
My flight leaves at 10:00 p.m. tonight.

01:24:41.159 --> 01:24:43.328
Take care of Seok-ryu.

01:24:45.455 --> 01:24:46.790
I did hope it might happen.

01:24:47.957 --> 01:24:48.792
But who knew?

01:24:48.875 --> 01:24:50.877
How did you get my number?

01:24:50.960 --> 01:24:54.047
I asked Mr. Yoon and he gave it to me.

01:24:54.130 --> 01:24:55.465
[sighs] Myeong-u, seriously?

01:24:57.842 --> 01:25:00.470
I'll bring Seok-ryu over.
You can say goodbye.

01:25:02.055 --> 01:25:03.973
I can't give you a lot of time though.

01:25:04.599 --> 01:25:06.142
Keep it short and simple.

01:25:06.643 --> 01:25:07.727
Keep your distance too.

01:25:09.229 --> 01:25:10.396
I'll keep that in mind.

01:25:11.106 --> 01:25:12.899
Also, thank you.

01:25:14.275 --> 01:25:15.235
For staying…

01:25:16.194 --> 01:25:17.445
by her side back then.

01:25:26.955 --> 01:25:28.581
[mellow music continues playing]

01:25:31.334 --> 01:25:32.210
Go ahead.

01:25:33.378 --> 01:25:34.712
Hey, Choisseung.

01:25:34.796 --> 01:25:39.592
I'm more petty, immature,
and impatient than you think.

01:25:41.803 --> 01:25:43.805
But I think this is right.

01:25:45.723 --> 01:25:46.933
Go ahead.

01:26:05.535 --> 01:26:06.619
[chuckles softly]

01:26:07.662 --> 01:26:11.166
We've already said our goodbyes.
He went overboard, don't you think?

01:26:11.791 --> 01:26:13.501
I'm grateful he did it though.

01:26:14.127 --> 01:26:18.214
I mean, I would've dressed up
if I knew I was coming here.

01:26:18.339 --> 01:26:20.633
It's the last time you'll see me,
and I look terrible.

01:26:22.093 --> 01:26:22.969
You're beautiful.

01:26:24.387 --> 01:26:26.264
I've never seen you shine so bright.

01:26:28.266 --> 01:26:29.184
Thanks.

01:26:31.436 --> 01:26:33.521
Also, thank you for everything.

01:26:35.023 --> 01:26:36.107
I'm more thankful.

01:26:38.026 --> 01:26:40.153
Should we shake hands for one last time?

01:26:41.487 --> 01:26:44.532
I know someone's watching,
but I think it'll be okay.

01:26:53.416 --> 01:26:54.417
Jeez.

01:26:55.501 --> 01:26:56.586
[Hyeon-jun] Be happy.

01:26:57.337 --> 01:26:58.338
[sighs]

01:26:58.421 --> 01:26:59.964
Don't get sick again.

01:27:01.549 --> 01:27:03.635
Yeah, you too.

01:27:04.719 --> 01:27:06.930
I hope you meet someone nice.

01:27:10.975 --> 01:27:12.352
It seems like you already have.

01:27:15.688 --> 01:27:17.732
I really don't like him.

01:27:20.318 --> 01:27:21.486
But he's all right.

01:27:24.822 --> 01:27:25.823
I'm off.

01:27:33.456 --> 01:27:34.457
[pop song playing]

01:28:14.622 --> 01:28:15.581
[Seok-ryu sniffles]

01:28:20.837 --> 01:28:21.838
[sniffles]

01:28:24.757 --> 01:28:25.758
[exhales]

01:28:30.638 --> 01:28:32.015
What are you doing?

01:28:32.598 --> 01:28:34.726
It's hot in here.

01:28:34.809 --> 01:28:36.102
Can you hold it for me?

01:28:40.064 --> 01:28:41.733
[Seok-ryu] What am I, a coat rack?

01:28:41.816 --> 01:28:43.526
Just do it, will you?

01:28:44.360 --> 01:28:46.112
Just stay like that for a second.

01:28:58.166 --> 01:29:00.418
BOARDING

01:29:02.587 --> 01:29:04.589
LOS ANGELES

01:29:04.672 --> 01:29:06.049
[airplane whooshes]

01:29:12.138 --> 01:29:14.140
[Seok-ryu] With Seung-hyo's
thoughtfulness,

01:29:14.724 --> 01:29:16.100
I cried for a long time that day.

01:29:20.104 --> 01:29:21.272
After a while,

01:29:22.106 --> 01:29:23.691
I emerged with swollen eyes

01:29:24.609 --> 01:29:27.403
and walked out that door with him.

01:29:32.784 --> 01:29:36.287
BEAR IN THE CAVE

01:29:36.371 --> 01:29:43.336
MOUTH OF THE CAVE

01:29:43.669 --> 01:29:45.588
[pop song continues playing]

01:30:28.131 --> 01:30:31.134
Subtitle translation by: Sue Mounce
